hin 10 feet of the kitchen, visible, mounted no higher than 5 feet, and either under 1 year old or tagged by a NJ certified fire equipment contractor","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request received 14+ business days before change of occupant","amount":"$66.00"},{"label":"Request received 8 to 13 business days before","amount":"$74.00"},{"label":"Request received 4 to 7 business days before","amount":"$106.00"},{"label":"3 business days or less notice","amount":"$171.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection after a failed inspection","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf$t$, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.lawnside.net/DocumentCenter/View/412/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (lawnside.net)"},{"url":"https://www.lawnside.net/DocumentCenter/View/464/Smoke-Alarm-Detector-Application-for-2025-PDF","label":"Official source (lawnside.net)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Regional Fire Prevention Alliance of Barrington, New Jersey serves the Municipalities of Barrington, Hi-Nella, Lawnside, Mt. Ephraim and Oaklyn.$t$, $t$febef68fd7229a023a762f6f2b62d324e0a5333217962f555546a7e38024c34c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":11,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0421.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0421.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0422$t$, $t$Lindenwold Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Continued Occupancy (CCO); Certificate of Transfer of Title (CTT) for vacant or rehab properties$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Lindenwold Construction Office / Code Enforcement (Housing Clerk)","Contact: 856-783-2121 ext. 224 · hprotich@lindenwold.net","Apply: Not stated as a fixed deadline. The fee is lower if the inspection is scheduled 10 or more business days out. For a vacant CTT, call 5 to 7 business days before settlement for a pre-inspection.","How to apply: Fill out the one-page CCO application and submit it to the Code Enforcement Office at 15 N. White Horse Pike with a check or money order payable to the Borough of Lindenwold. Fees are per unit and nonrefundable. The Borough calls the listed contact to schedule after the permit and zoning search is done. A failed inspection needs a new application and fee before reinspection. For vacant or rehab pr","No open building or zoning permits (must be closed with fees paid)","No work done without a required construction or zoning permit","No unsafe structures or unsafe conditions","10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on every level and outside each sleeping area","CO alarm within 10 feet of sleeping areas","2A-10B:C fire extinguisher under 10 lbs, mounted within 10 ft of kitchen, tagged with current receipt","House numbers at least 4 inches, contrasting, fixed to the house and visible from the street","Handrails on 3 or more risers; guardrails on porches/decks 30 inches or higher","GFCI within 6 ft of water; no bare-wire fixtures","Heat, appliances (anti-tip on range), hot and cold water and toilets working","Water heater relief valve discharge pipe 2 to 6 inches from floor","Bathroom window or exhaust fan","No holes, flaking paint or water stains on walls, ceilings, floors; no roof leaks","Yard free of trash, debris and junk vehicles; all code violations abated","Utilities on at time of inspection","Also: Open permits must be closed: No open building or zoning permits; must be fully satisfied with fees and inspections before the CCO is issued.","Also: Work without permits: Unpermitted work (commonly finished basements, water heaters, furnaces) must be permitted and inspected before the CCO is issued.","Also: Zoning check: The Borough runs a zoning approval and permit search before scheduling the CCO inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"CCO inspection, 1-2 units, scheduled over 10 days out (form: 10 or more business days), per unit","amount":"$75"},{"label":"CCO inspection, scheduled less than 10 days out (form: 4 to 10 business days), per unit","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Re-inspection, per unit","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Administration fee for changing inspection date or unit number more than once","amount":"$20"},{"label":"Certificate of Transfer of Title (vacant property), includes one re-inspection within 120 days","amount":"$125"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.lindenwoldnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/140/Residential-Property-Sales---Inspection-Application--CCO-Certificate-of-Continued-Occupancy-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.lindenwoldnj.gov/178/Code-Enforcement-Housing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.lindenwoldnj.gov/178/Code-Enforcement-Housing","label":"Official source (lindenwoldnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.lindenwoldnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/140/Residential-Property-Sales---Inspection-Application--CCO-Certificate-of-Continued-Occupancy-PDF","label":"Official source (lindenwoldnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.lindenwoldnj.gov/DocumentCenter/View/141/Residential-Property-Sales---Inspection-Application--CTT-Certificate-of-Title-Transfer--for-Vacant-or-Rehab-Properties-PDF","label":"Official source (lindenwoldnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All sales of a property must file for a certificate of occupancy (C/O) inspection for smoke detectors, carbon monoxide detectors, fire extinguishers, and house numbers.$t$, $t$fd0ed06a71bffef85a2c907375a88bb398f5c6a0c453a0079d1d5a1e985c1100$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0422.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0422.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0422$t$, $t$Lindenwold Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Lindenwold Fire District No. 1, Bureau of Fire Prevention (fire district)","Contact: 856-346-0935 · firemarshal@lindenwoldfire.com","Apply: Submit request 3 to 4 weeks before settlement","How to apply: Submit the online Residential Inspection Request Form on lindenwoldfire.com. Pay at the time of inspection by check or money order (no cash). The certificate is issued at the inspection if the home passes and payment is received. No temporary certificates.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 5/26/2026: Timothy D Shannon · (856) 346-0935 · tshannon@lindenwoldfire.com","10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on every level; hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Basement alarm at bottom of stairwell on the ceiling, not between joists","Bedroom hallway smoke alarms within 10 feet of all bedroom doors","Smoke and CO alarms less than 10 years old and working","CO alarm in hallway within 10 feet of all bedrooms; not in switched outlets","Low-voltage alarm systems must be tested by an alarm contractor before the inspection, with the certificate shown to the inspector","House numbers at least 4 inches, contrasting, fixed to the house, visible from the street or 50 feet (Borough Ordinance No. 757)","Homes with a secondary power source (solar, generator, battery storage) need a permanent printed label at the main panel and meter, e.g. \"Caution: Multiple Sources of Power\"","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request received 8 or more calendar days before settlement","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Request received 7 calendar days before settlement","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Request received 3 calendar days or less before settlement","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.lindenwoldfire.com/FormCenter/General-Forms-4/Residential-Inspection-Request-Form-46$t$, $t$https://www.lindenwoldfire.com/182/Smoke-Carbon-Monoxide-Alarm-Compliance-C$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.lindenwoldfire.com/182/Smoke-Carbon-Monoxide-Alarm-Compliance-C","label":"Official source (lindenwoldfire.com)"},{"url":"https://www.lindenwoldfire.com/DocumentCenter/View/198/Residential-Resale-Requirements---","label":"Official source (lindenwoldfire.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$When selling a one or two family home in Lindenwold, you must obtain a Certificate of Smoke Alarm and Carbon Monoxide Detector Compliance CSACMAPFEC 5:70-2.3 (a) prior to the settlement. Please submit your request for inspection 3 to 4 weeks prior to the settlement date.$t$, $t$1cd6aba66e0cf7c34c5e8ae8a3c94a0e37a860074d4f1352cf684b1250fb7b15$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":10,"q_ok":10,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0422.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0422.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0423$t$, $t$Magnolia Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Change in Ownership (Chapter 112 Certificates of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Magnolia Construction Office","Contact: 856-783-1520"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.magnolia-nj.org/construction/page/certificate-change-ownership$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.magnolia-nj.org/construction/page/certificate-change-ownership","label":"Official source (magnolia-nj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.magnolia-nj.org/municipal-clerk/page/notice-final-adoption-ordinance-12-2026","label":"Official source (magnolia-nj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Certificate of Change in Ownership Inspections are required whenever a home is being sold$t$, $t$2977f92d8b7df35139ad23cc01ea30cc9e33f86e214559598889f126f9080d4d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0423.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0423.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0423$t$, $t$Magnolia Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Magnolia Construction Office (smoke detector compliance) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-783-1520","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 5/22/2026: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.magnolia-nj.org/construction/page/certificate-change-ownership$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$SMOKE DETECTOR COMPLIANCE Name: Magnolia Boro Constr Office Addr: 438 West Evesham Av Magnolia NJ 08049 Phone (856) 783-1520$t$, $t$15a8ef2048d26cacbc7c3bcb637378d16afe326b697e37d710d40b1c89b8b98b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0423.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0423.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0424$t$, $t$Merchantville Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Inspection / Resale Certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Merchantville Code Enforcement (Office of Code Enforcement and Rental Housing Inspection)","Contact: 609-413-0010 · codeenforcement@merchantvillenj.gov","How to apply: Complete the Resale Inspection Application (includes the smoke detector certificate application) and bring it to the Borough Clerk's office at 1 W. Maple Avenue to pay the fee. Code Enforcement then contacts the applicant to schedule the inspection.","Valid for: 6 months after passed inspection","House numbers visible from the street","Fences, decks, sheds and accessory structures must have proper permits","Sidewalks and driveways level and free of trip hazards","Smoke alarm on each level including basement; 10-year sealed lithium battery type","CO detector within 10 feet of sleeping areas (plug-in or battery OK)","2A:10BC fire extinguisher in a cabinet or on a hanger within 10 feet of the kitchen","Handrail on stairs with more than 4 risers; guards on surfaces more than 30 inches above grade","Exterior surfaces painted or protected and in good repair","Yard free of excess weeds, rubbish and garbage","Accessory structures (garages, fences, walls) sound and in good repair","Pools clean; pools over 24 inches deep fenced at least 48 inches with self-closing, self-latching gates","Also: Permits for accessory structures: All fences, decks, sheds, and accessory structures must have proper permits."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Resale re-inspection","amount":"$10.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/RESALE%20PAPERWORK%201-2026.pdf?t=202601211210300$t$, $t$https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/government/code_enforcement_and_rental_inspection.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/government/code_enforcement_and_rental_inspection.php","label":"Official source (merchantvillenj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/RESALE%20PAPERWORK%201-2026.pdf?t=202601211210300","label":"Official source (merchantvillenj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Before the sale of all residential properties, you are required to obtain a Resale Inspection, including smoke detector compliance. Please bring your completed application to the clerk's office with you to pay the required fee. The Applicant will be contacted to schedule an inspection.$t$, $t$74f5f0ace975924cbfc056fb8bf819d8f63e8ea20f9b815220ec8caab1ed1e08$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":7,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0424.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0424.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0424$t$, $t$Merchantville Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Merchantville Code Enforcement (Certificate of Smoke Detector Compliance) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-662-2474 ext. 310 · codeenforcement@merchantvillenj.gov","Apply: Fee is lowest if applied for more than 10 business days before settlement","How to apply: Fill out the Borough 'Application for Certificate of Smoke Detector Compliance' (page 3 of the resale packet) and submit it with the resale application at the Clerk's office with payment. The Code Enforcement Official schedules the inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 3/17/2026: Kevin Patti · (856) 662-0900 · kpatti@merchantvillenj.gov","Each smoke alarm must be a 10-year sealed lithium battery detector, on every level including basements","CO detector within 10 feet of sleeping areas","2A:10BC extinguisher in an approved cabinet or on a hanger within 10 feet of the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"More than 10 business days before settlement","amount":"$35.00"},{"label":"Less than 10 days but more than 4 days","amount":"$70.00"},{"label":"4 business days or fewer","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, each","amount":"$10.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/RESALE%20PAPERWORK%201-2026.pdf?t=202601211210300$t$, $t$https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/government/code_enforcement_and_rental_inspection.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/RESALE%20PAPERWORK%201-2026.pdf?t=202601211210300","label":"Official source (merchantvillenj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.merchantvillenj.gov/government/code_enforcement_and_rental_inspection.php","label":"Official source (merchantvillenj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$BOROUGH OF MERCHANTVILLE APPLICATION FOR CERTIFICATE OF SMOKE DETECTOR COMPLIANCE$t$, $t$5e50de1b76d2499e392e576b131afcb5958e6993146a050a32ec8b2be881af6f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":7,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0424.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0424.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0425$t$, $t$Mount Ephraim Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (Certificate of Continued Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Construction / Zoning / Code Enforcement Office","Contact: 856-931-1546 ext. 205 · tweiss@mountephraim-nj.com","Apply: Application and fee must be received before an inspection can be scheduled; no set number of days published","How to apply: Complete the Application for Resale CO Inspection and submit it with the fee (cash or check payable to 'Borough of Mount Ephraim'). If mailing, address it to 'Attn: Construction', 121 S. Black Horse Pike, Mount Ephraim, NJ 08059. After the office receives the form and payment, call to schedule the inspection. Contact 856-931-1546 ext. 205 or tweiss@mountephraim-nj.com.","Exterior: visible 911 house number, steps, walkways, ramps, guardrails, handrails","Exterior: obstructions and hazards, perimeter grading, gutters, spouts and splash blocks","Basement or crawl space: foundation openings, secure weatherproof accesses, vapor barrier, mold","Sump pump: electrical connection, backflow preventer, discharge","Interior: infestation (mice, insects), handrails, guardrails, bathroom venting (fan or window)","GFCI receptacles in kitchen and bath","Garage, flooring, kitchen, bath condition","Switch and receptacle covers, electrical fixtures, panel box and panel covers, A/C disconnect","Window glass, operable egress windows, window guards","Water heater: chimney connection, relief valve and floor discharge","Water pipes, drain pipes, fixtures, toilet mounting, hot and cold water controls","Heating system","All open permits must be closed before the CO is issued","Also: Open permits must be closed: No CO will be issued until all open permits have been closed.","Also: Temporary certificate of occupancy fee: Ordinance 2024-15 sets $30 for the first issuance and renewal of a temporary certificate of occupancy."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Single family dwelling resale CO","amount":"$120.00"},{"label":"Certificate of continued occupancy, 1-2 family residence under 5,000 sq ft (Ordinance 2024-15)","amount":"$120"},{"label":"Reinspection, 1-2 family residence (Ordinance 2024-15 certificate of occupancy section)","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.mountephraim-nj.com/page/construction-office-zoning-resale-inspections/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211229005949/https://mountephraim-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Application-for-Resale-CO-inspection.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211229010006/https://mountephraim-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Resale-Inspection-Checklist-003.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20241112171805/https://mountephraim-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Ord.-2024-15-Construction-Codes-Uniform.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$*Please Note*: No CO will be issued until all open permits have been closed. Application and fee must be received prior to scheduling any inspection.$t$, $t$01b512f9cb49402d5bd214fa1396d211b1d8dd4c66209fe9683bda67bfbfd71b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0425.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0425.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0425$t$, $t$Mount Ephraim Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Regional Fire Prevention Alliance (Barrington) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-547-0991 · firealliance@barringtonboro.com","Apply: 14 or more business days before the change of occupant for the lowest fee; weekends, holidays and the settlement date do not count","How to apply: Fill out the Regional Fire Prevention Alliance smoke detector certification application and email it to firealliance@barringtonboro.com, or print it and drop it in the mailbox at 205 Haines Avenue, Barrington, NJ 08007. Include a check or money order payable to 'Regional Fire Prevention Alliance'. Walk-in office hours Tuesday to Friday 8am to 2pm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 8/5/2026: Nicholas D'Alonzo · (856) 547-0991 · ndalonzo@barringtonboro.com","Smoke alarms by construction date: pre-1975 homes need 10-year sealed battery alarms on each level including basement; newer homes need AC powered interconnected alarms per the era table","All smoke alarms must be less than 10 years old; someone must take them down and check the date on the back, and undated alarms must be replaced","Low voltage (alarm company) fire alarm systems must be tested by an alarm contractor before inspection, with the certification shown to the inspector","CO alarm within 10 feet of sleeping areas if the home has a fuel burning appliance, fireplace or attached garage; CO alarms must be less than 7 years old","House numbers: Arabic numerals at least 3 inches tall, contrasting, mounted at least 60 inches above ground and visible from the street","Secondary power source warning label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and meter if there is a generator, solar, or battery storage","Everything must be done before the inspector arrives; an adult (18+) must be present at the start of the time block","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request received 14+ business days before change of occupant","amount":"$66.00"},{"label":"Request received 8-13 business days before","amount":"$74.00"},{"label":"Request received 4-7 business days before","amount":"$106.00"},{"label":"Request received 3 business days or less before","amount":"$171.00"},{"label":"Reinspection after a failed inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Penalty for change of ownership or occupancy without the certificate","amount":"$500"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf$t$, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20211229005949/https://mountephraim-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/Application-for-Resale-CO-inspection.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Regional Fire Prevention Alliance of Barrington, New Jersey serves the Municipalities of Barrington, Hi-Nella, Lawnside, Mt. Ephraim and Oaklyn.$t$, $t$9ea7ed350f15974bc9ef564d14346fc87b82d94ff98a413f691264430cf1ecac$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0425.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0425.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0426$t$, $t$Oaklyn Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Compliance (resale property maintenance inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Code Department / Code Enforcement","Contact: 856-858-2457","How to apply: The 2018 borough Certificate of Compliance form was submitted to Borough Hall, 500 White Horse Pike, Oaklyn, NJ 08107 (tel. 856-858-2457, fax 856-854-0180). Confirm the current form and process with Borough Hall, since the current borough website could not be read.","Valid for: 90 days, provided the seller has not changed","Sidewalks, walkways, driveways and driveway aprons safe: no cracks, raised or deteriorated concrete (asphalt allowed for driveways only, not aprons or sidewalks)","Handrails where there are 3 or more steps; steps 30 inches above grade need a handrail on one side; spindles no more than 4 inches apart","Railings on porch or stoop perimeters that have none, with spindles no more than 4 inches apart","Peeling, chipping or unpainted exterior surfaces scraped and painted","Broken window panes repaired","Open electrical splices or improperly installed fixtures corrected","Gutters and downspouts connected and in place","Any obvious hazardous and maintenance conditions","Sump pump must not be connected to the sewer; Public Works inspects before settlement","Also: Sump pump sewer connection inspection by Public Works: Per Oaklyn Ordinance 108-22 no sump pump can be connected to the sewer system; Public Works inspects before settlement."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Property maintenance inspection (2018 form)","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/5cd08893-258d-4063-980b-adf6716d47d7/downloads/Resale%20Application.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.oaklyn-nj.net/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://img1.wsimg.com/blobby/go/5cd08893-258d-4063-980b-adf6716d47d7/downloads/Resale%20Application.pdf","label":"Official source (img1.wsimg.com)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200808231550/https://oaklyn-nj.net/permits-%26-forms","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$According to the Borough of Oaklyn Ordinance 11-00, Chapter 101, Section 101-3. A Certificate of Compliance inspection is required upon the sale of all properties. The Certificate is good for (90) days provided the seller has not changed.$t$, $t$2d1836abd8a51c1920a9f39dbd15e2e1aba76a41bac455d0b54a74b3081a54cc$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":5,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0426.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0426.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0426$t$, $t$Oaklyn Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Regional Fire Prevention Alliance (Barrington) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-547-0991 · firealliance@barringtonboro.com","Apply: 14 or more business days before the change of occupant for the lowest fee; weekends, holidays and the settlement date do not count","How to apply: Fill out the Regional Fire Prevention Alliance smoke detector certification application and email it to firealliance@barringtonboro.com, or print it and drop it in the mailbox at 205 Haines Avenue, Barrington, NJ 08007. Include a check or money order payable to 'Regional Fire Prevention Alliance'. Walk-in office hours Tuesday to Friday 8am to 2pm.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 8/5/2026: Nicholas D'Alonzo · (856) 547-0991 · ndalonzo@barringtonboro.com","Oaklyn ordinance 75-10A(4): at least one working smoke alarm inside each sleeping area, plus one outside each sleeping area enclosed by a door, within 10 feet (listed as 'Oaklyn Borough Residents Only' on the Alliance's 2022 form)","Smoke alarms by construction date: pre-1975 homes need 10-year sealed battery alarms on each level; newer homes need AC powered interconnected alarms per the era table","All smoke alarms must be less than 10 years old; undated alarms must be replaced","CO alarm within 10 feet of sleeping areas if there is a fuel burning appliance, fireplace or attached garage; CO alarms must be less than 7 years old","House numbers: Arabic numerals at least 3 inches tall, mounted at least 60 inches above ground, visible from the street","Secondary power source warning label within 18 inches of the main panel and meter where there is a generator, solar or battery storage","Alarm company systems must be tested by a contractor before inspection, with the certification shown to the inspector","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request received 14+ business days before change of occupant","amount":"$66.00"},{"label":"Request received 8-13 business days before","amount":"$74.00"},{"label":"Request received 4-7 business days before","amount":"$106.00"},{"label":"Request received 3 business days or less before","amount":"$171.00"},{"label":"Reinspection after a failed inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Penalty for change of ownership or occupancy without the certificate","amount":"$500"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf$t$, $t$https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/regional-fire-prevention-alliance/","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://barringtonboro.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Barrington-Smoke-Doc-update-Fillable-pdf.pdf","label":"Official source (barringtonboro.com)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230701064007/https://mountephraim-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/Smoke-and-Carbon-Monoxide-Alarm-Packet.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Regional Fire Prevention Alliance of Barrington, New Jersey serves the Municipalities of Barrington, Hi-Nella, Lawnside, Mt. Ephraim and Oaklyn.$t$, $t$b40ca95daf1a5729bfb83799c3bf2452d394f03c242825ec1cda363849169138$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":5,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0426.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0426.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0427$t$, $t$Pennsauken Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing Resale Certificate of Inspection (Housing Resale CO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Department of Housing / Property Maintenance","Contact: 856-665-1000 ext. 1411 · spaul@pennsauken.gov","Apply: No fixed number of days published. The town says to leave enough time between the inspection and settlement so the certificate is issued before settlement.","How to apply: Complete the Housing Resale & Fire Certificate Inspection application (PDF) or apply online through the township's GovPilot portal. Submit the form with the $175 fee (cash, check or money order payable to Pennsauken Township) to the Municipal Building, Attn: Housing / Property Maintenance Dept., 5605 N. Crescent Blvd., Pennsauken, NJ 08110. The inspection is scheduled once the form and fee are rec","Interior and exterior housing resale inspection of every 1 and 2 family dwelling","Grading and drainage, sidewalks and driveways, accessory structures","Stumps from trees that caused sidewalk damage","Exterior structure: protective treatment, structural members, foundation walls, roofs and drainage","Roof certification and chimney certification (wood burning or gas) may be required","Stairways, decks, porches and balconies; handrails and guards","Interior surfaces, stairs and walking surfaces","Infestation / termite","Plumbing system hazards and plumbing certification","Mechanical appliances and mechanical certification","Electrical hazards and electrical certification; 2 outlets in every bedroom; GFCI style protection near sinks, sump pump, bathrooms, kitchen counters; weather resistant covered outdoor outlets","Smoke alarms, carbon monoxide detector, interior locked doors","Shed letter if there is a shed; grass or weeds","Rental registration if the property will be rented","New or open permits must be closed; no new occupancy until the final CO is issued","Also: Open and required construction permits must be closed: All permits must be obtained, inspected and pass inspection before the final Certificate of Inspection is issued. Construction dept: 856-665-1000 x129, building@pennsauken.gov.","Also: Temporary CO by buyer affidavit: Buyer may sign a notarized Affidavit for a Temporary CO, accepting responsibility for violations; must be delivered to Housing before settlement.","Also: Rental registration if buyer will rent: Checklist item 251.19 rental registration required; 1-2 family rentals register annually and are inspected."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Housing Resale CO plus Fire Certificate, combined application fee","amount":"$175.00"},{"label":"Housing Resale Certificate of Inspection portion","amount":"$100"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1116/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Application-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.pennsauken.gov/194/Housing-Property-Maintenance$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/194/Housing-Property-Maintenance","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1154/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Information-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1406/Housing-Resale-Inspection-Checklist-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1116/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$For Residential Housing Sales, A housing resale CO and fire certificate is required for every transfer of ownership for all one and/or two-family dwellings. To obtain the CO and fire certificate the property must pass a housing resale inspection.$t$, $t$725fd8d0ff63f789c08276c21d37c3ca33bd13e4b07b58b064d485e486204997$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0427.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0427.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0427$t$, $t$Pennsauken Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pennsauken Township Department of Housing / Property Maintenance (Fire Certificate issued with the Housing Resale CO) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-665-1000 ext. 1411 · spaul@pennsauken.gov","How to apply: Same combined application as the Housing Resale CO. Submit the Housing Resale & Fire Certificate Inspection application with the $175 total fee to the Housing / Property Maintenance Dept., 5605 N. Crescent Blvd., or apply online via GovPilot.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/18/2026: Steven Schwegel, Jr. · (856) 665-0774 · sschwegel@pennsaukenfire.org","Each level must have an AC hard wired or 10-year sealed battery smoke alarm; all smoke alarms must be within 10 years of manufacture date","Alarm type depends on original construction date: pre-1975 homes need 10-year sealed battery alarms on each level; newer homes need hard wired interconnected alarms per the era table","A smoke alarm is required in every bedroom regardless of the home's age, plus outside sleeping areas and on every level","Smoke alarm at the bottom of basement stairs (within 10 feet of the stairway, not in the stairway) and top of walk-up attic stairs","Carbon monoxide alarm within 10 feet of each sleeping area","Hard-wired proprietary fire alarm systems must be tested per NFPA 72 with a test report at inspection","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Fire Certificate portion of combined resale application","amount":"$75"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1116/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Application-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.pennsauken.gov/194/Housing-Property-Maintenance$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1154/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Information-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1115/Smoke-Alarm-Carbon-Monoxide-Detector-Fire-Extinguisher-Instructions-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pennsauken.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1116/Housing-Resale-And-Fire-Cert-Inspection-Application-PDF","label":"Official source (pennsauken.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The housing resale and fire inspections are completed by the township housing department inspectors.$t$, $t$e90a9fe012694bf693ddaedeb7cdd7d16772ce874789c30769f7fb260619a33e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0427.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0427.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0428$t$, $t$Pine Hill Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$verify$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not confirmed yet: Watchdog could not confirm online whether Pine Hill Borough requires a resale certificate. Call the office before closing.","Also: Rental registration and inspection (if the buyer will rent): All residential rental properties must be registered and inspected before occupancy, then annually or on each change of occupancy."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.pinehillboronj.com/departments/construction-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240718161949/https://www.pinehillboronj.com/departments/construction-office/","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$To obtain a Certificate of Occupancy (C.O.) for the resale of a property, please contact the Pine Hill Fire Department: (856) 783-8666.$t$, $t$ff1575778e6ce44f02dfe077113d9ed5dfd9a041280798f81f130cf863e9cb56$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0428.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0428.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true),
  ($t$0428$t$, $t$Pine Hill Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Pine Hill Fire District #1, Bureau of Fire Prevention (fire district)","Contact: 856-784-0030 · firemarshal@pinehillfiredistrict.com","Apply: More than 10 business days before the inspection date for the lowest fee; inspections are done one day a week","How to apply: Fill out the application in the Smoke Detector Inspection Packet and mail it or drop it off with a check or money order (no cash) at the Bureau of Fire Prevention, 1109 Erial Road, Pine Hill, NJ 08021. The form and payment must be received before an appointment is scheduled; the office then contacts you. If dropping off, put it in the mailbox and send a follow-up email. The office is part time, so","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 3/5/2026: Robert Fowler · (856) 784-0030 · firemarshal@pinehillfiredistrict.com","Power to the house must be on before scheduling, or an approved Special Circumstance form (extra fee, plus a follow-up inspection or electrician letter before anyone moves in)","Smoke alarm on every level within 15 feet of the bedrooms","Smoke alarms older than 10 years must be replaced before inspection","Hardwired smoke alarms must stay and cannot be replaced with battery alarms","CO alarm in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedroom doors; CO alarms older than 7 years must be replaced; not plugged into switched outlets or near floor molding","Fire extinguisher rated 2A10BC (5 lbs), brand new or dated/tagged for the current year, mounted visibly within 10 feet of the kitchen or toward an exit from the kitchen","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"More than 10 business days before inspection","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"5 to 9 business days before inspection","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"4 or less business days before inspection","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$20.00"},{"label":"Special Circumstance (power off with hardwired alarms): additional fee on top of the normal fee, same tiers, e.g. 10+ business days","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Penalty for occupying without the required follow-up inspection (Special Circumstance cases)","amount":"$500.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://pinehillfiredistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Smoke-Detector-Inspection-Packet.pdf$t$, $t$https://pinehillfiredistrict.com/department-list/inspection-office/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://pinehillfiredistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Smoke-Detector-Inspection-Packet.pdf","label":"Official source (pinehillfiredistrict.com)"},{"url":"https://pinehillfiredistrict.com/department-list/inspection-office/","label":"Official source (pinehillfiredistrict.com)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240718161949/https://www.pinehillboronj.com/departments/construction-office/","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Application for Certification of Smoke Detector and carbon Monoxide Alarm Compliance as required by N.J.A.C 5:70-2.3, based upon the amount of time remaining before the date of inspection as follows:$t$, $t$1e8f1451a9bc084414b81713d95c4c51b492cb0e120bef2ee5509f799a25eacb$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0428.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0428.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true),
  ($t$0430$t$, $t$Runnemede Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Continued Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Office of Code Enforcement / Construction and Code Enforcement","Contact: 856-939-2815","Apply: Apply at least 10 working days before settlement or occupancy","How to apply: Download the Residential CCO application (3 pages, including a swimming pool affidavit), complete it, and submit it with a check to the Office of Code Enforcement, 24 N. Black Horse Pike, Runnemede, NJ 08078. Call 856-939-2815 with questions.","Valid for: Application expires 90 days after inspection if the CCO has not been issued","House number visible from the street, at least 4 inches tall","Steps free of cracks and trip hazards, even treads and risers, closed risers (4 inch ball rule)","Sidewalks, aprons and driveways level with no cracks or lifts over 1/2 inch; driveway parking surface must be impervious (no stone or gravel)","Graspable handrail on steps with 4 or more risers; guardrails where porch, landing or stairs are over 30 inches above grade","Property free of debris and hazards; abandoned tanks and wells removed with a permit","No peeling paint or rust on exterior surfaces","Gutters and downspouts secure and clear, with splash blocks or diverters","Foundation openings sealed; basement and crawlspace windows intact; Bilco doors and crawlspace access working and sealed","Exterior receptacles, including garages and sheds, GFCI protected","Window glass intact; electric service cable secured; damaged wiring and fixtures replaced","Approved chimney cap","Zoning and construction permits for additions, pools, sheds, garages, decks and fences; open permits must be closed","Swimming pool: bonding/grounding certificate from a licensed NJ electrician dated within 30 days of the application, plus pool affidavit","Also: Open construction permits must be closed before sale: Any permits without final inspection or certificate of approval must be closed out before the CCO is issued; permits are required for any work done without permits.","Also: Swimming pool affidavit and bonding certificate: Pool affidavit is page 3 of the residential CCO application; a bonding/grounding certificate from a licensed NJ electrician dated within 30 days is required if there is a pool."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential dwelling CCO application","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Reinspection, after the first reinspection (residential)","amount":"$25.00"},{"label":"Commercial / Multi Family CCO application (may apply to a 2-family sale; not confirmed)","amount":"$150.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://runnemedenj.org/documents/add-document/department-documents/construction/certificate-of-continued-occupancy/69-construction-form-residential-cco/file$t$, $t$https://runnemedenj.org/departments/construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://runnemedenj.org/documents/add-document/department-documents/construction/certificate-of-continued-occupancy/68-exterior-compliance-requirements-for-a-certificate-of-continued-occupancy-for-the-sale-of-a-single-family-dwelling/file","label":"Official source (runnemedenj.org)"},{"url":"https://runnemedenj.org/documents/add-document/department-documents/construction/certificate-of-continued-occupancy/69-construction-form-residential-cco/file","label":"Official source (runnemedenj.org)"},{"url":"https://runnemedenj.org/departments/construction","label":"Official source (runnemedenj.org)"},{"url":"https://runnemedenj.org/documents/add-document/department-documents/construction/certificate-of-continued-occupancy/70-construction-form-commercial-multi-family-cco/file","label":"Official source (runnemedenj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$EXTERIOR COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS Certificate of Continued Occupancy for the sale of a single-family dwelling. FORM ISSUE DATE, 07/17/2020$t$, $t$1e11cfe83b87aa53532e36887be0f7eec2a5f5de9b85c3309ebd7ae5bdf93012$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0430.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0430.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0430$t$, $t$Runnemede Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Runnemede Bureau of Fire Prevention, Office of the Fire Marshal (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-939-2817","Apply: Schedule at least 8 days ahead for the lowest fee","How to apply: Request a Smoke Detector & Carbon Monoxide Alarm inspection through the borough's SDL online portal (linked from the Fire Prevention / Inspections page). The March 2025 paper application said fees are payable to the Borough of Runnemede by check or money order, no refunds.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/22/2026: Michael Kearney · (856) 939-2817 · Mkearney@runnemedenj.org","Smoke alarm requirements depend on the year the home was built (pre-1977 battery alarms on each level; later eras need 120V hardwired, interconnected alarms as listed in the borough table)","Where no alarms exist or battery alarms are being replaced, use 10-year sealed battery alarms; hardwired alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Smoke alarms must not be over 10 years old from date of manufacture","Alarms must be mounted with proper hardware; nails, thumbtacks, tape or Velcro are not acceptable","Carbon monoxide alarm in the hall outside bedrooms, no more than 10 feet from any bedroom","Monitored alarm systems in homes built 1977 or later must be maintained at change of occupancy","Secondary power source label ('CAUTION: MULTIPLE SOURCES OF POWER') within 18 inches of the main panel and meter if the home has a generator, solar panels or battery storage","The borough states that since February 2025 a fire extinguisher is no longer required for the certificate","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Appointment scheduled at least 8 days before inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Appointment scheduled less than 8 but more than 4 days before inspection","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Appointment scheduled less than 4 days before inspection","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Penalty for not obtaining the certificate before sale or change of occupancy","amount":"$500"}]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://runnemedenj.org/public-safety/fire-prevention$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://runnemedenj.org/documents/add-document/department-documents/fire-prevention/847-requirements-for-smoke-alarms-for-one-and-two-family-residences/file","label":"Official source (runnemedenj.org)"},{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250803120942/https://runnemedenj.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/CSDCMAC-Application-2025.pdf","label":"Official source (web.archive.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$To apply for a Smoke Detector & Carbon Monoxide Alarm inspection, scan the code below: Or visit www.runnemedenj.org/public-safety/fire-prevention$t$, $t$c0657c6ad38e2b734f6b944ff38b537b6d1fb2a49adbb73ae98c49690961fc86$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0430.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0430.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0431$t$, $t$Somerdale Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Compliance / Certificate of Continued Occupancy (CCO), Residential Safety Inspection$t$, $j$["Issued by: Office of the Fire Marshal (Somerdale Fire Prevention Bureau)","Contact: 856-783-6320 ext. 2100 · dmarx@somerdale-nj.com","Apply: Apply 11 or more working days before settlement for the lowest fee","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Certificate of Compliance, Single Family Dwelling completely and submit it with a check or money order payable to the Somerdale Fire Prevention Bureau. Contact the Fire Marshal's office at 856-783-6320 ext. 2100 or dmarx@somerdale-nj.com. Borough Hall is at 105 Kennedy Blvd, open Mon to Thu 8 AM to 5:15 PM, closed Friday.","A representative must be on location for the inspection","Lead paint certification for any house built before 1978 (application form; the guideline sheet labels this as for rental properties)","House numbers in Arabic lettering, 3 inches, on the front wall or porch, 30 inches above ground","Smoke alarm on each floor and in each bedroom; 10-year sealed battery alarms where none exist or when replacing battery alarms; hardwired alarms may not be replaced with battery alarms","Carbon monoxide detector on each floor","2A/10BC fire extinguisher, not over 10 lbs, wall mounted about 5 ft from the ground (waist level accepted), within 10 ft of the kitchen and in view","Sidewalks and driveways with no cracks or unevenness, no skim coating or ramping; must be visible and clear of snow, ice and parked cars","Front and rear porch or deck well maintained and sturdy","Windows operable and in decent condition","Firmly secured railing on stairs with 4 or more steps","Water check: toilets flush, drains work, hot water","Covers on all light switches and receptacles","No holes in walls, floors or ceilings; painted","Sump pump must not be tied into the sewer","Yard and property maintained (grass cut, trimmed)","Also: Open permits must be closed: Any open permits must be closed / finalized; solar panels and EV chargers must have been permitted.","Also: Lead paint certification for pre-1978 homes: The single family application states any house built before 1978 must have a lead paint certification provided (citing N.J. P.L. 2021, c. 182, the rental lead law)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Single family, 11+ working days before settlement","amount":"$70.00"},{"label":"Single family, 4 to 10 working days before settlement","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Single family, 1 to 3 working days before settlement","amount":"$161.00"},{"label":"Reinspection (each)","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Single-Family-Dewelling.pdf$t$, $t$https://somerdale-nj.com/departments/fire-marshal/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/departments/fire-marshal/","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/departments/construction/","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Single-Family-Dewelling.pdf","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Guidelines.pdf","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Office of the Fire Marshal is responsible for inspections not only for Special Events, but inspections prior to a new business opening as well as Certificate of Occupancy inspections prior to settlement on the purchase of a home or renting to a tenant.$t$, $t$705d594caa3f377f19706ae0e1f2c25215fa95423a53dfadea35ab84a41c0a3c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0431.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0431.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0431$t$, $t$Somerdale Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Somerdale Office of the Fire Marshal / Somerdale Fire Prevention Bureau (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-783-6320 ext. 2100 · dmarx@somerdale-nj.com","Apply: 11 or more working days before settlement for the lowest fee","How to apply: Same application as the CCO: submit the Single Family Dwelling Certificate of Compliance application with a check or money order payable to the Somerdale Fire Prevention Bureau.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 3/9/2026: David Marx · (856) 783-6320 · dmarx@somerdale-nj.com","Smoke alarm on each floor and in each bedroom","10-year sealed battery alarms where no alarms exist or when replacing battery alarms; hardwired alarms must not be replaced with battery alarms","Carbon monoxide detector on each floor","2A/10BC fire extinguisher, not to exceed 10 lbs, wall mounted about 5 ft from the ground (waist level accepted), within 10 ft of the kitchen, in view","Secondary power source labels on electric panel and meter (as of 2/3/25) where solar or generators exist","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined CCO and smoke/CO/extinguisher inspection, 11+ working days before settlement","amount":"$70.00"},{"label":"Combined inspection, 4 to 10 working days","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Combined inspection, 1 to 3 working days","amount":"$161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Single-Family-Dewelling.pdf$t$, $t$https://somerdale-nj.com/departments/fire-marshal/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Guidelines.pdf","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://somerdale-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Single-Family-Dewelling.pdf","label":"Official source (somerdale-nj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$FIRE EXTINGUISHER (INSTALLED 5 FT. FROM GROUND, MOUNTED ON THE WALL, WITHIN 10 FT OF THE KITCHEN IN VIEW OF PUBLIC) (MOUNTED WAIST LEVEL IS ACCEPTED) MUST BE A 2A/10BC FIRE EXTINGUISHER, not to exceed 10lbs.$t$, $t$9b97fe02518325ffda41346b4f5c663d3497e50bf59b94dc47fe70c486416c89$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0431.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0431.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0432$t$, $t$Stratford Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$verify$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not confirmed yet: Watchdog could not confirm online whether Stratford Borough requires a resale certificate. Call the office before closing.","Contact: 856-783-0600 · codeenforcement@stratfordnj.org"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://stratfordnj.org/code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://library.municode.com/nj/stratford_borough/codes/code_of_ordinances","label":"Official source (library.municode.com)"},{"url":"https://stratfordnj.org/borough-forms/","label":"Official source (stratfordnj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$No person, group of persons, association, partnership or corporation or any combination thereof who owns, manages, conducts or operates a dwelling unit shall rent, lease, let, sublet or permit the same to be occupied or re-rented by another without first securing from the public officer of the borough a certificate of occupancy for said dwelling unit.$t$, $t$94879c0de55787c97fc8220f14c686c87284301a14260081a539f3ffd9520277$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0432.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0432.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true),
  ($t$0432$t$, $t$Stratford Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ Department of Community Affairs, Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: 609-633-6106","How to apply: Apply and pay online through the NJ DCA service portal: click 'Apply for Smoke Certification' at firesolutions.dca.nj.gov.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 2/2/2023: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application more than 10 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application 4 to 10 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application fewer than 4 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://stratfordnj.org/pdf/forms/DCA-Smoke-Fire-CO.pdf","label":"Official source (stratfordnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/divisions/dfs/codes/regulations/adopted_amendment_5_10_2.9.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All Certificates of Occupancy for the Borough of Stratford will now be handled by the New Jersey Department of Community Affairs (DCA). You can access their service portal at: https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/$t$, $t$0b2fa556a8f7e56bbe30b64e761d2a06d264e5e3a4f0e51b65e8ed671beceb3b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0432.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0432.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true),
  ($t$0433$t$, $t$Tavistock Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$verify$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not confirmed yet: Watchdog could not confirm online whether Tavistock Borough requires a resale certificate. Call the office before closing.","Contact: 856-429-0039 · clerk@tavistocknj.org"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://tavistocknj.org/whos-who/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://tavistocknj.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/2024-Tavistock-Minutes-12-19-2024.pdf","label":"Official source (tavistocknj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resolution #34-2024 Authorizing Shared Service Agreement with Haddonfield - Construction$t$, $t$e29a39aa4bab30d925f62a77523bd89caad711111454c0103c8ea5f8e4cdb372$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online","no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0433.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0433.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online; no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0433$t$, $t$Tavistock Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Haddonfield Bureau of Fire Prevention (serving Tavistock under a shared service agreement) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-429-4308 · ebusch@haddonfield-nj.gov","How to apply: Contact the Haddonfield Fire Official (Ernest F. Busch) or the Haddonfield Construction and Zoning Office, Room 104, Haddonfield Borough Hall, which receives smoke detector compliance forms and payment for Haddonfield. Confirm the Tavistock process and fee before applying.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 5/18/2026: Ernest F Busch · (856) 429-4308 · ebusch@haddonfield-nj.gov","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.haddonfieldnj.org/government/departments/fire_department/smoke_detector___sidewalk_inspection_requests/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://tavistocknj.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/2024-Tavistock-Minutes-12-19-2024.pdf","label":"Official source (tavistocknj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resolution #33-2024 Authorizing Shared Service Agreement with Haddonfield - Fire Services$t$, $t$32289d3f06f96ad625972dda57860410a519cb0676b6b7e5404350c18009cd41$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online","no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0433.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0433.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online; no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0434$t$, $t$Voorhees Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Residential Resale Certificate (Residential Change of Owner)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Voorhees Planning & Zoning Department","Contact: 856-429-0647 · resales@voorheesnj.com","Apply: Fee depends on how soon the inspection is requested after the application is submitted: more than 10 business days is the lowest fee. Submit the signed and sealed survey early (one issued within the past 60 days is recommended).","How to apply: Fill out the Residential Resale Application and send it to the Planning & Zoning Department by email (resales@voorheesnj.com), through the SDL online portal, or in person at 2400 Voorhees Town Center. Pay by cash or check payable to Voorhees Township. Include the buyer, agent and certificate email, lock box details, and the survey.","Valid for: 60 days after issue if settlement or occupancy has not occurred","Recent signed and sealed survey for all single family homes (not required for condos); one issued within the past 60 days is recommended","All open construction permits must be closed before the certificate is issued","House number on the building itself, at least 30 inches above ground, at least 3 inches tall, on a contrasting background, visible from the street; stick-on numbers not accepted","Carbon monoxide alarm outside and within 10 feet of every sleeping area; extra alarm if a bedroom is on another level or more than 10 feet away","Smoke alarms on every level including the basement and outside sleeping areas; battery-only alarms must be 10-year sealed units","A hardwired or monitored alarm system cannot be replaced with battery-only alarms; monitored systems must be put in test mode for the inspection","No zoning violations; any addition, shed, deck, fence or other improvement built without zoning or construction permits must be legalized first","Pool fencing and gates must meet Section 305 of the International Swimming Pool and Spa Code","Someone must be present unless the property is completely empty; inaccessible areas fail the inspection","Tax assessor property record card is checked during the inspection","Also: Open permits must be closed: The resale form requires Township sign-off that all outstanding permits for the property have been closed and finalized before the certificate is issued.","Also: Survey: A current signed and sealed survey must be reviewed before the Resale Certificate can be issued (single family homes; not condos)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection requested more than 10 business days after application","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Inspection requested 2 to 10 business days after application","amount":"$125.00"},{"label":"Inspection requested 1 to 2 business days after application","amount":"$150.00"},{"label":"Inspection requested the same day as application","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"First re-inspection (also charged when any part of the property is inaccessible)","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Each later re-inspection","amount":"$150"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://voorheesnj.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Residential-Resale-Application-7.02.2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://voorheesnj.com/departments/zoning/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://voorheesnj.com/departments/zoning/","label":"Official source (voorheesnj.com)"},{"url":"https://voorheesnj.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Residential-Resale-Application-7.02.2026.pdf","label":"Official source (voorheesnj.com)"},{"url":"https://voorheesnj.com/departments/construction/","label":"Official source (voorheesnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.vtfd66.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/townshipord2023.pdf","label":"Official source (vtfd66.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$If you are selling your home, the presence of an unpermitted improvement (a violation) may delay settlement since a resale certificate cannot be issued for a transfer of ownership while a violation exists.$t$, $t$44c8206de455a7f99e5775151ea73919fedbddaa719c3c6163d8ea61bc278ed7$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0434$t$, $t$Voorhees Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Voorhees Township Planning & Zoning Department (residential smoke/CO inspections, done with the resale certificate inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-429-0647 · resales@voorheesnj.com","Apply: Same as the resale certificate; see resale fee tiers","How to apply: Use the Residential Resale Application from the Zoning Department; the smoke and CO alarm check is part of that inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 5/26/2026: Thomas O'Brien · (856) 783-6630 · tom.Obrien@vtfd66.org;","Battery-only smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed units (per Voorhees resale packet and Fire Department page)","Carbon monoxide alarm within 10 feet of each sleeping area","Hardwired or monitored alarm systems cannot be downgraded to battery-only alarms","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://voorheesnj.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Residential-Resale-Application-7.02.2026.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.vtfd66.org/fire-prevention/inspection-bureau/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.vtfd66.org/fire-prevention/inspection-bureau/","label":"Official source (vtfd66.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$SMOKE DETECTOR INSPECTIONS FOR RESIDENTIAL PROPERTIES ARE COMPLETED THROUGH THE VOORHEES TOWNSHIP ZONING DEPARTMENT.$t$, $t$e1ed6dd1b39ed6e07c61d4cee5cff9fdeceafd81cb960b907574638f9f548298$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0434.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0435$t$, $t$Waterford Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Residential Reoccupancy Inspection (Residential Resale Inspection); Certificate of Inspection$t$, $j$["Issued by: Waterford Township (form posted by the Construction & Zoning Enforcement office; inspections under the Township fire official)","Contact: 856-768-2300 ext. 307 · fireofficial@waterfordtwp.org","Apply: Apply at least 10 days before settlement for the lowest fee","How to apply: Fill out the Residential Reoccupancy Form (block, lot, settlement date, lock box code and location, owner, buyer and realtor contacts) and submit it to Waterford Township, 2131 Auburn Ave, Atco, NJ 08004. Pay by cash, check or money order. Include passed water and septic certifications.","Valid for: 30 days","Smoke alarm on each floor including the basement and within 10 feet of a bedroom","Battery smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed; hardwired (110 volt) alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Smoke alarms less than 10 years old (or per manufacturer replacement date)","Carbon monoxide alarm within 10 feet of a bedroom, less than 5 years old (or per manufacturer)","House number visible from the street, 3 to 6 inches tall","Passed water and septic certifications must be submitted before the certificate is released","A house with a cesspool cannot be sold until a septic system is installed; if a new system is needed, show money in escrow","Secondary power (meter and electrical panels) and all utilities on and working (listed on the 2025 form)","No bulk trash or debris left at the property or curb (2025 form says the certificate will not be issued otherwise)","Do not take Township trash and recycling carts","Uninhabitable 'as is' sales need a notarized letter and are referred to the Construction Office (2025 form)","Also: Water and septic certifications: Passed water and septic certifications must be submitted before the Township releases the certificate (mark public water, private well, public sewer or septic).","Also: Cesspool replacement: A house with a cesspool cannot be sold until a septic system is installed; if a new system is needed, proof of escrowed funds is required."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection, applied 10 days before settlement","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Inspection, applied 4 to 9 days before settlement","amount":"$125"},{"label":"Inspection, applied 2 to 3 days before settlement","amount":"$200"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://waterfordtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Reoccupy-APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://waterfordtwp.org/departments/construction-zoning-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://waterfordtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Reoccupy-APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (waterfordtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://waterfordtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Scanner@Waterfordtwp.org_20250820_102823.pdf","label":"Official source (waterfordtwp.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$***PASSED WATER AND SEPTIC CERTIFICATIONS MUST BE SUBMITTED BEFORE WE RELEASE CO***$t$, $t$add18ae1162dce1dd5c75a62f3a31995a49e3a279c47ba16bb18a09efb53a13b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0435.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0435.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0435$t$, $t$Waterford Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Waterford Township Fire Prevention (municipal local enforcing agency, Fire Official Craig Fallstick) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-768-2300 · fireofficial@waterfordtwp.org","Apply: Apply at least 10 days before settlement for the lowest fee; certificate good for 30 days","How to apply: Use the Township Residential Reoccupancy Form; the smoke and CO alarm certificate is issued from that inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 8/17/2026: Craig Fallstick · (856) 768-2300 · fireofficial@waterfordtwp.org","Smoke alarms less than 10 years old (or per manufacturer replacement date)","Carbon monoxide alarms less than 5 years old (or per manufacturer replacement date)","Battery smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed; hardwired alarms cannot be swapped for battery units","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Same combined resale/reoccupancy inspection fee, applied 10 days before settlement (pay once)","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Same combined inspection fee, applied 4 to 9 days before settlement (pay once)","amount":"$125"},{"label":"Same combined inspection fee, applied 2 to 3 days before settlement (pay once)","amount":"$200"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://waterfordtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Reoccupy-APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://waterfordtwp.org/departments/construction-zoning-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://waterfordtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Reoccupy-APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (waterfordtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A Certificate of Inspection will only be issued when the premises meet the minimum requirements of the New Jersey State Uniform Fire Code, N.J.A.C. 5:70-4:19.$t$, $t$8686371fb0b1b3a14a0aa294b700cfa38efc856310f833fecf3a4274cff038a3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":8,"fee_ok":8,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0435.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0435.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0436$t$, $t$Winslow Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate / Certificate of Continued Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Winslow Township Construction Office (Housing Office)","Contact: 609-567-0700 option 5 · construction@winslowtownship.com","Apply: Payment must come with the application; check payments need a 10 working day hold before the inspection can be done","How to apply: Complete the Resale Certificate Application (seller, buyer, both agents, settlement date, block and lot) and submit it with payment to the Housing Office, Township of Winslow, 125 South Route 73, Braddock, NJ 08037. Attach well and septic certifications if they apply. Schedule the inspection by calling 609-567-0700, option 5 (Monday to Friday, 8:30 am to 4:30 pm).","Well water: passing test by an NJDEP certified lab (Private Well Testing Act), or Camden County Health Dept. letter of approval for a new well","Septic: Camden County Health Dept. letter of compliance (no future action), or certificate of compliance for a new system","Property must comply with all Township and State codes and ordinances (the office links the 2015 International Property Maintenance Code)","Sidewalks and driveway aprons are the owner's responsibility and must meet Township ordinances","All open permits closed with final inspections (for example water heater, A/C, furnace, finished basement)","Dwelling must be fit for human habitation","Certificate issued only when all requirements are met","Separate fire (smoke/CO) certificate from the Winslow Township Fire District is also required","Also: Well and septic certifications: If the property has a well or septic system, the certifications must accompany the Township resale application (NJDEP certified lab well test or County Health letter; County Health septic compliance letter).","Also: Open permits must be closed: All open permits must be closed with final inspections before the Township issues the certificate.","Also: Sidewalks and aprons: Sidewalks and driveway aprons are the homeowner's responsibility and must comply with Township ordinances."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential inspection (includes 1 free re-inspection)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Commercial inspection (includes 1 free re-inspection)","amount":"$200"},{"label":"Each re-inspection after the first free re-inspection","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.winslowtownship.com/filestorage/3308/3536/3538/3540/RESALECERTIFICATE.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.winslowtownship.com/content/3298/3503/default.aspx$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.winslowtownship.com/content/3298/3503/default.aspx","label":"Official source (winslowtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.winslowtownship.com/filestorage/3308/3536/3538/3540/RESALECERTIFICATE.pdf","label":"Official source (winslowtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://www.ecode360.com/35704976","label":"Official source (ecode360.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Our office also performs rental inspections and CCO inspections for resale property, Monday thru Friday.$t$, $t$4fd35c85d76822035e22170701048f832afd9a7330a5d49460713c91b9d19458$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":9,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0436.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0436.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0436$t$, $t$Winslow Township$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Winslow Township Fire District No. 1 (Winslow Township Fire Department), Fire Prevention Division / Office of the Fire Marshal (fire district)","Contact: 609-561-4225 · firedistrict@winslowtwpfd.org","Apply: Apply 3 to 4 weeks before closing (recommended); fee depends on days of notice; certificate valid 90 days from inspection","How to apply: Apply online on the Fire District website and then pay through the linked Edmunds WIPP payment page, or download the packet and fax it to 609-561-5823, or apply in person at the Fire District Office, 9 Cedar Brook Road, Sicklerville (Monday to Friday, 9 am to 5 pm). Staff call within 24 hours to schedule. Inspections are on Tuesdays and Thursdays in a morning or afternoon block. Pay by check (paya","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 2/6/2026: Joseph G Hahn · (609) 561-4225 · josephh@winslowtwpfd.org","Every smoke alarm must be less than 10 years old; take each alarm down and check the date on the back","Battery (DC) smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed units","Hardwired (110 volt) interconnected alarms must all sound when one is tested; AC power must be on or no inspection is done; replacing a hardwired alarm with a battery unit fails","Smoke alarm type and number depend on the year built (for example 1991 to present: hardwired with battery backup on each level and in each bedroom, interconnected)","CO alarm outside of but within 10 feet of all sleeping areas if there is any fuel-burning appliance, fireplace or attached garage","Homes with a secondary power source (solar, generator, battery storage) need a permanent, not handwritten, 'Caution: Multiple Sources of Power' label at the main panel and the electric meter (ANSI Z535.4)","Monitored low-voltage fire alarm systems must be tested and certified by an alarm contractor before the inspection; bring the certificate","An adult (18+) must be present for the whole inspection; no lockbox entry","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Application, 8 or more days advance notice","amount":"$65.00"},{"label":"Application, 4 to 7 days advance notice","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Application, 3 or fewer days notice","amount":"$150.00"},{"label":"Senior citizen (62 or older, proof of age attached) discount line","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection (per visit)","amount":"$35.00"},{"label":"Missed appointment","amount":"$35.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://winslowtwpfd.org/online-resale-application$t$, $t$https://winslowtwpfd.org/fire-marshal-office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://winslowtwpfd.org/vertical/sites/%7B2458775F-59B7-4354-B7A0-12D3BE8EC490%7D/uploads/Smoke_Application_2025.pdf","label":"Official source (winslowtwpfd.org)"},{"url":"https://www.winslowtownship.com/filestorage/3308/3536/3538/3540/RESALECERTIFICATE.pdf","label":"Official source (winslowtownship.com)"},{"url":"https://winslowtwpfd.org/history","label":"Official source (winslowtwpfd.org)"},{"url":"https://winslowtwpfd.org/fire-marshal-office","label":"Official source (winslowtwpfd.org)"},{"url":"https://winslowtwpfd.org/vertical/sites/%7B2458775F-59B7-4354-B7A0-12D3BE8EC490%7D/uploads/CSDCMACPFE_Instructions_4.15.2025.pdf","label":"Official source (winslowtwpfd.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$CERTIFICATIONS ARE VALID FOR 90 DAYS FROM THE DATE OF INSPECTION$t$, $t$95a5678fef3f7357cc590d949878fa1dd730ef1a8a27bd3fe4a1656a517c70c4$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":9,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":9,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0436.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0436.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0437$t$, $t$Woodlynne Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Inspection for Resale$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Woodlynne Construction Official","Contact: 856-962-8300 ext. 219 · woodlynnedavid@comcast.net","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Certificate of Inspection for Resale (address, owner, agent, emergency contact) and return it to the Borough of Woodlynne, 200 Cooper Ave., Woodlynne, NJ 08107, or fax it to 856-962-8763. Contact David Munoz at 856-962-8300 ext. 219.","Inspection for resale is marked pass or fail by the Construction Official","Any building, plumbing, electrical or fire permits the Construction Official requires must be completed before the final Certificate of Occupancy"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Application fee","amount":"$96.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.woodlynnenj.org/_files/ugd/b7bd99_79e91dc4d3fa4e6a9fcbfd5848ff3881.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.woodlynnenj.org/code-enforcement$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.woodlynnenj.org/_files/ugd/b7bd99_79e91dc4d3fa4e6a9fcbfd5848ff3881.pdf","label":"Official source (woodlynnenj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.woodlynnenj.org/code-enforcement","label":"Official source (woodlynnenj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Application for Certificate of Inspection for Resale$t$, $t$afc2f014c99884691b3c2547c41675f030de8ff43ea8a668fb326192c7ffa992$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":6,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0437.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0437.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0437$t$, $t$Woodlynne Borough$t$, $t$CAMDEN$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: NJ Department of Community Affairs, Division of Fire Safety, Bureau of Fire Code Enforcement (NJ DCA, state)","Contact: 609-633-6106","How to apply: Apply and pay online through the NJ DCA service portal using 'Apply for Smoke Certification'.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (NJ DCA, state), updated 3/14/2023: Louis Kilmer · (609) 633-6132","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application more than 10 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application 4 to 10 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, application fewer than 4 business days before change of occupant (state fee rule, 2017)","amount":"$161.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://firesolutions.dca.nj.gov/ultra-fire-home/smoke-application-create/$t$, $t$https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/offices/bfce.shtml$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/state_towns%207_17_26.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/fire%20directory_county%20summary/fire_code_enforcement_director.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.nj.gov/dca/divisions/dfs/codes/regulations/adopted_amendment_5_10_2.9.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$WOODLYNNE BORO 0437 SC$t$, $t$1b07455fdcef50dd8ab38a2241ec97ce3f733cac148fb309db11f4756b552ba2$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":4,"quotes":6,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0437.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0437.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0801$t$, $t$Clayton Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (resale and rental)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Clayton Construction Office","Contact: 856-881-2882 ext. 118","Apply: No set lead time published. The form says not to schedule settlement until the CO is approved and returned, and the violation notice gives 90 days to correct items and says to allow ample time before settlement.","How to apply: Fill out the Certificate of Occupancy Application for Resales and Rentals (mark House Sale) and submit it to the Construction Office at 125 N. Delsea Drive, Clayton, with the fee paid by cash or check. Incomplete applications are not accepted.","House number at least 4 inches, contrasting, visible for 911","Curb, sidewalk and driveway apron level and repaired","Roof, chimney, fireplace, HVAC and water heater may need certification if deficient (HVAC and water heater age base 15 years)","Exterior grounds cleared of debris and trailers, cars or trucks","Gutters, downspouts and splash blocks where needed","Electric service line, meter and panel in good repair","Steps, decks, porches, guardrails (4 inch spacing, 36 inches high) and graspable handrails built to code","Pool fence with self-closing gate","Smoke detectors on every floor including basement","Carbon monoxide detectors on all levels, including by bedrooms","Portable fire extinguisher, A:B:C type, no larger than 10 lb, wall mounted, visible, within 10 feet of the kitchen","Keyless exit deadbolts on exterior doors","Water heater relief valve discharge within 6 inches of floor","Bathroom, kitchen and dryer venting (dryer ducts 4 inch metal); GFI outlets in kitchen, bath, laundry and exterior","Stove anti-tip device; working windows and screens; sound walls, ceilings, floors; attic and basement not used as habitable space","Also: Radio water meter check: CO checklist item 47 lists 'Radio Water Meter' and says to call DPW to replace the meter.","Also: Sump pump discharge: CO checklist item 48 asks 'Sump Pump Discharge to Sewer?'","Also: Recycling container: CO checklist item 46 lists 'Recycling Container'."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection (resale or rental)","amount":"$65"},{"label":"Third inspection","amount":"$25"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.claytonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/474/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application-Form-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.claytonnj.com/1266/Certificates-of-Occupancy$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.claytonnj.com/1266/Certificates-of-Occupancy","label":"Official source (claytonnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.claytonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/474/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application-Form-PDF","label":"Official source (claytonnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.claytonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/476/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Violation-Notice-Checklist-here-PDF","label":"Official source (claytonnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Certificates are required for both residential and commercial properties each time there is a change in tenant and/or owner.$t$, $t$2a6b68d5da13055c34d970e665859fcd2083a0c253b21e72382c559cc8529005$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0801.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0801.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0801$t$, $t$Clayton Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Clayton (smoke alarm and CO alarm application handled through the Construction Office line, ext. 118) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-881-2882 ext. 118","Apply: Fee is due at application. Inspections are Tuesday and Thursday, 11:30am to 2:30pm. Days are counted from the date the request is received to the closing date; applications after 4:00pm count from the next business day.","How to apply: Fill out the Borough of Clayton Application for Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm and Secondary Power Source Identification Label Compliance with the closing date, and pay the fee when you apply at 125 N Delsea Drive.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 6/16/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","The CO checklist asks for an A:B:C residential fire extinguisher no larger than 10 pounds, mounted on the wall, visible, within 10 feet of the kitchen","The CO checklist asks for carbon monoxide detectors on all levels, basement, first floor and second floor by bedrooms","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection or re-inspection","amount":"$125.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.claytonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/5311/Smokes-and-CO-Applicaton$t$, $t$https://www.claytonnj.com/1219/Construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.claytonnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/5311/Smokes-and-CO-Applicaton","label":"Official source (claytonnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$BOROUGH OF CLAYTON 125 N Delsea Drive Clayton, NJ 08312 856-881-2882 ext:118 APPLICATION FOR SMOKE ALARM, CARBON MONOXIDE ALARM & SECONDARY POWER SOURCE IDENTIFICATION LABEL COMPLIANCE (CSACMASPICL)$t$, $t$57ad96db81161d1f2cfe328d315fea98293203185e014b5cd36d64b7dc31d68d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0801.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0801.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0802$t$, $t$Deptford Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing Change in Ownership inspection / Certificate of Occupancy (Continued Certificate of Occupancy)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Deptford Township Construction Office, Housing Inspector","Contact: 856-845-5300 · constructioninspections@deptford-nj.org","Apply: Allow ten business days for the inspection to be completed","How to apply: Apply online through the Township's SDL portal (linked from the Construction page as the way to apply for a Housing Certificate of Occupancy), or complete the Application for Housing Change in Ownership (mark Resale) and leave it in the drop box outside the Municipal Building at 1011 Cooper Street. Get the Deptford Township MUA approval stamp on the form. Call (856) 845-5300 to schedule the inspec","Valid for: Inspections are valid for 60 days","Inspection of the entire property under the International Property Maintenance Code, current edition","Inspection under Change in Occupancy rules N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3 and 4.19 (smoke alarm, CO alarm and fire extinguisher rules) and Township Ordinance 0.2.15","All open construction permits must be completed and closed out before the certificate is issued","Any compliance order or notice of violation must be corrected before the home can be sold or rented","Homes on well or septic need a No Further Action letter from the Gloucester County Department of Health","Deptford Township MUA approval stamp on the application","Also: Deptford Township MUA approval: The resale application has a 'DEPTFORD TOWNSHIP MUA APPROVAL STAMP' box, and asks for the water meter location.","Also: Well or septic: County Health No Further Action letter: If the property has a well or septic, a No Further Action letter from the Gloucester County Department of Health is required before the certificate is issued.","Also: Open permits closed: All work on open construction permits must be completed and permits closed before the certificate of occupancy is issued."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Per unit, includes application, inspection and one re-inspection","amount":"$100 per unit"},{"label":"Each additional re-inspection, per unit","amount":"$75 per unit"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.deptford-nj.org/filestorage/34753/35668/35670/37913/2025_CHANGE_IN_OCCUPANT_APPLICATION__-_final.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.deptford-nj.org/construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.deptford-nj.org/filestorage/34753/35668/35670/37913/2025_CHANGE_IN_OCCUPANT_APPLICATION__-_final.pdf","label":"Official source (deptford-nj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.deptford-nj.org/construction","label":"Official source (deptford-nj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$APPLICATION FOR HOUSING CHANGE IN OWNERSHIP$t$, $t$20e371e5f3634d9543eaee086aac8f6ce259d9ea5549f93df3eaf5ea2b2adfc6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0802.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0802.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0802$t$, $t$Deptford Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Deptford Township Construction Office, Housing Inspector (checked as part of the Housing Change in Ownership inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-845-5300 · constructioninspections@deptford-nj.org","How to apply: No separate smoke certificate application was found. The Township resale housing application says the inspection is done under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3 and 4.19 (the state smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm and fire extinguisher rules). Under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3(a)1, where a town has its own resale inspection, a separate certificate is not required but the town may not issue its certificate until the home ","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 4/29/2025: Francis E Pote · (856) 848-3098 · fpote@deptfordfd.org","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.deptford-nj.org/filestorage/34753/35668/35670/37913/2025_CHANGE_IN_OCCUPANT_APPLICATION__-_final.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.deptford-nj.org/construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.deptford-nj.org/filestorage/34753/35668/35670/37913/2025_CHANGE_IN_OCCUPANT_APPLICATION__-_final.pdf","label":"Official source (deptford-nj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$An inspection of the entire property according to: Change in Occupancy Pursuant to N.J.A.C. 5:70 -2.3 and 4.19; Ordinance # 0.2.15 and International Property Maintenance Code, Current Edition$t$, $t$3ca42ec33cd355c16c75649b32399acb5d1810b78ce4bd5fb64e9f28dc62e8e0$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0802.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0802.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0803$t$, $t$East Greenwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for Resale and Rental Property (C.O. Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: East Greenwich Township Construction Department (Construction Official / Building Housing Inspector)","Contact: 856-423-0654 ext. 8132 · rsnyder@eastgreenwichnj.com","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Certificate of Occupancy (list the resale buyer and settlement date) and submit it to the Construction Department at 159 Democrat Road, Mickleton, which schedules the inspection. Pay by exact cash or check. Inspections are weekday mornings (the form says 8 to 11am; the web page says Monday to Thursday, 8 to 10am).","Housing code inspection of the whole home using the Township checklist (Property Maintenance Code based)","Smoke detectors on every level (basement, first and second floor) and outside each sleeping area","Since January 1, 2019, battery smoke detectors must be 10-year sealed battery units (hard-wired AC interconnected units do not need replacing)","Carbon monoxide alarms near sleeping areas; fire extinguisher in the proper place","All utilities on, all smoke and CO detectors working (they will be tested), pets restrained","Well certification and septic certification (Gloucester County approval) if applicable","Chimney certification if there is a wood-burning fireplace","Anti-tip bracket on the oven","All open construction permits must have passed inspections","Yard and grass maintained, house number posted, roof, gutters, walls, windows, screens, steps, porches, handrails and guardrails in good repair","Plumbing, heating, water heater and electric service working; bathroom ventilation; no junk or unregistered vehicles","Pool properly located and fenced","Also: Well and septic certification: Well certification and septic certification required if applicable; septic needs Gloucester County approval.","Also: Chimney certification: Application form: 'Woodburning fireplace: (chimney cert required)'.","Also: Open permits: All open construction permits must have inspections and must pass inspections.","Also: Utilities on: All utilities must be turned on for the inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"C.O. inspection, residential, per unit","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"First re-inspection","amount":"$45.00"},{"label":"Each re-inspection after the first","amount":"$70.00"},{"label":"Fee stated on the Construction web page (conflicts with the form)","amount":"$45.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KFkcT1ccswtj1lABto9y31QmLIX_Qg9O/view?usp=sharing$t$, $t$https://www.eastgreenwichnj.com/government/construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.eastgreenwichnj.com/government/construction","label":"Official source (eastgreenwichnj.com)"},{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KFkcT1ccswtj1lABto9y31QmLIX_Qg9O/view?usp=sharing","label":"Official source (drive.google.com)"},{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fyG7txo9ueioQiCUTrqTHq5-3JPFfoIi/view?usp=sharing","label":"Official source (drive.google.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All changes of occupancy (commercial, residential and rental) will require an inspection before a new Certificate of Occupancy can be obtained. Applications are available at the construction office and inspections can be scheduled with them.$t$, $t$6d27cddbbd06fe231c97b3654cf73f326c14c70cb1a3a82bf674955ae5eec636$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":6,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0803.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0803.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0803$t$, $t$East Greenwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: East Greenwich Township Construction Department (checked as part of the resale C.O. housing inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-423-0654 ext. 8132 · rsnyder@eastgreenwichnj.com","How to apply: No separate smoke certificate application was found. The Township C.O. inspection checklist includes 'NJAC 5:70-4.19 Smoke detectors, carbon monoxide alarms, and fire extinguisher located in appropriate areas'. Under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3(a)1, where a town has its own resale inspection, a separate certificate is not required but the town may not issue its CO until the home meets 5:70-4.19. Confirm wit","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 8/5/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Township checklist: as of January 1, 2019 all battery smoke detectors must be 10-year sealed battery single station alarms; AC interconnected alarms do not need replacing","Smoke detectors on every level including basement and outside each sleeping area; basement detector near the bottom of the basement stairs","Carbon monoxide alarms in the immediate vicinity of sleeping areas","Fire extinguisher placement is checked on the C.O. inspection","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KFkcT1ccswtj1lABto9y31QmLIX_Qg9O/view?usp=sharing$t$, $t$https://www.eastgreenwichnj.com/government/construction$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fyG7txo9ueioQiCUTrqTHq5-3JPFfoIi/view?usp=sharing","label":"Official source (drive.google.com)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$NJAC 5:70-4.19 Smoke detectors, carbon monoxide alarms, and fire extinguisher located in appropriate areas$t$, $t$bf1e45c1d05cee14a8afc7a1f900f33fd6ff4fef84eb6bb6cece167989665a19$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":1,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":6,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":4},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0803.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0803.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0804$t$, $t$Elk Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (C/O inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Elk Township Construction Office, Housing Official","Contact: 856-881-6525 ext. 118 · construction@elktownshipnj.gov","Apply: 30 days advance notice before settlement is required","How to apply: Fill out the Certificate of Occupancy Application and give it to the Construction Office at 680 Whig Lane, Monroeville (in person, in the vestibule drop box, or by mail) with a check payable to 'Elk Township'. Apply at least 30 days before settlement. Inspections are Mondays and Wednesdays; late applications get no special treatment. If the home is sold 'as is', the buyer can sign the Township's n","Valid for: 3 months if the property is occupied, 6 months if vacant","Well water: passing test by an NJDEP certified lab (Private Well Testing Act), or County Health letter for a new well","Septic: Gloucester County Health Dept letter of Compliance-No Further Action, or License to Operate for a new system","Cesspools, privies and outhouses must be replaced with a septic system before transfer (limited exceptions)","Smoke detector in each bedroom and on every level (10 year sealed device)","Smoke and CO detectors outside bedrooms, within 10 feet of bedrooms","General condition of interior, exterior, grounds and accessory buildings (sheds, barns, garages)","Roofing, siding, trim, window glass, screens and doors","Pipes and traps under sinks; heater and water heater","Chimney condition; chimney certification for wood fireplaces, wood stoves or pellet stoves","GFCI outlets within 6 feet of water in kitchens, bathrooms and laundry","4 inch reflective house numbers","Township-issued trash and recycling containers on the premises","No open construction permits","Also: Well water test: Passing well water test by an NJDEP certified lab (NJAC 7:9E, Private Well Testing Act), or County Health Dept approval letter for a new well.","Also: Septic certification / cesspool replacement: Gloucester County Health Dept letter of Compliance-No Further Action (or License to Operate for new systems). Cesspools, privies and outhouses must be replaced with a septic system on transfer, with limited exceptions (NJAC 7:9A-3.16(b)).","Also: No open construction permits: Open construction permits must be closed.","Also: Township trash and recycling containers: Township-issued trash and recycle containers are required to be on the premises.","Also: As-is sale buyer letter: For homes sold 'as is', the buyer signs a notarized letter agreeing to finish required repairs within 60 days; a Settlement Document is issued when the letter is received."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"First and second inspection","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Each additional inspection request","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/Documents/How%20Do%20I/Find%20Municipal%20Forms/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/departments/construction.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/Documents/How%20Do%20I/Find%20Municipal%20Forms/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (elktownshipnj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$30 DAYS ADVANCE NOTICE, PRIOR TO SETTLEMENT OR ANY CHANGE OF OCCUPANCY IS REQUIRED FOR C/O INSPECTIONS$t$, $t$8ac5e92fae7f0093c0c9bd38ee3471591c0b480e3eb7e81abb4c4b4ed008d678$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0804.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0804.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0804$t$, $t$Elk Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Elk Township Construction Office, Housing Official (smoke and CO alarms checked on the resale C/O inspection) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-881-6525 ext. 118 · construction@elktownshipnj.gov","Apply: 30 days before settlement (same as the C/O inspection)","How to apply: No separate smoke certificate application was found. The smoke and CO alarm check is part of the Township C/O inspection. Under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3(a)1, where a town has its own resale inspection, a separate certificate is not required but the town may not issue its CO until the home meets N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19. Ask the Construction Office whether a portable fire extinguisher is also checked, since the","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 6/17/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Township CO form: smoke detector in each bedroom and on every level of the house, 10 year sealed device","Township CO form: smoke and CO detectors outside bedrooms within 10 feet of bedrooms","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/Documents/How%20Do%20I/Find%20Municipal%20Forms/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/departments/construction.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.elktownshipnj.gov/Documents/How%20Do%20I/Find%20Municipal%20Forms/Certificate-of-Occupancy-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (elktownshipnj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke detector required in each bedroom and on every level of house (10 yr sealed device)$t$, $t$fd0b2942a43fae0e76f176486401ceb9bc82426958601a2055dcf1667047048d$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0804.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0804.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0805$t$, $t$Franklin Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate / New Tenant Certificate (Certificate of Occupancy Transfer, Township Code Chapter 178)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Franklin Township Housing Code Official (Zoning and Land Use Department)","Contact: 856-694-1234 · housinginspector@franklintownship.com","Apply: File at least 30 days before settlement (the information sheet says allow a minimum of three weeks and suggests applying when the house is listed)","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Resale Certificate or New Tenant Certificate and hand it in with the fee at the Housing Code Official's Office in the Municipal Building, 1571 Delsea Drive, Franklinville. Applications and fees are not accepted in the field. There is a box on the form for a Non-Occupy (AS IS SALE) certificate request. If the buyer is taking over responsibility for the certificate, noti","Valid for: Applications are non-transferable and expire after 60 days","Passing water test and Gloucester County Board of Health septic approval","Reflective house numbers at least 3-1/2 inches high, readable from the street","Pool and yard fences with self-latching, out-swing gates (48 inch minimum height, 54 inch if latch at top)","Guardrails on landings or porches 30 inches or higher (36 inch minimum height, 4 inch spacing); sound stairs, decks, porches and balconies","No broken or missing glass; all windows with screens that open, close and lock","Stove anti-tilt device; all utilities on at inspection","Smoke detector on each level, in all bedrooms and outside each sleeping area (battery allowed)","Carbon monoxide detectors near sleeping areas (unless no fuel-burning device or attached garage)","ABC fire extinguisher at least 2A:10B:C, no more than 10 lbs, mounted in a visible, convenient spot","Handrails on stairs with four or more risers; bathroom window or exhaust fan","No electrical hazards or extension-cord wiring; GFCI at pools, spas, exterior, garage, kitchen, bath and within 5 feet of water","Plumbing vented and working; heat to all habitable rooms; water heater relief valve pipe ending within 6 inches of floor","Certifications may be required for roof, electrical, structural, heating or lead","Also: Well water test and septic approval: A passing water test and Gloucester County Board of Health septic approval are required before a Resale Certificate is issued.","Also: Records check: The office checks zoning, property, construction and violation records when processing the application (office-use section of the form).","Also: Buyer assumption of certificate: Under Chapter 178-4 the buyer may waive the seller's responsibility and take over getting the certificate, in writing filed with the Housing Code Official."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Each re-inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Fines for not getting approval within 30 days of initial inspection (per day)","amount":"$100.00 - $200.00 per day"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/6409/Application-for-Resale-Certificate-or-New-Tenant-Certificate-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/152/Code-Enforcement-Land-Use$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/6381/Resale-and-New-Tenant-Certificate-Information-and-Checklist-PDF","label":"Official source (franklintownshipnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/6409/Application-for-Resale-Certificate-or-New-Tenant-Certificate-PDF","label":"Official source (franklintownshipnj.org)"},{"url":"https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/179/Ordinance-024-14---Amending-Chapter-178---Certificate-of-Occupancy-Transfer-PDF","label":"Official source (franklintownshipnj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A Resale Certificate / New Tenant Certificate is required in the Township of Franklin each time a residential dwelling unit changes occupant and tenant.$t$, $t$2cefbf16b5f6d1ca072bd8821cac5af11acf25121bd3067cba70be27c28434da$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0805.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0805.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0805$t$, $t$Franklin Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Franklin Township (municipal fire code enforcing agency, Fire Marshals); alarms and extinguisher are checked on the Township Resale Certificate inspection (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-694-1234 ext. 6","How to apply: No separate smoke certificate application or fee was found. The smoke alarm, CO alarm and fire extinguisher items are on the Township Resale Certificate checklist. Under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3(a)1, where a town has its own resale inspection, a separate certificate is not required but the town may not issue its certificate until the home meets N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19. Confirm with the Fire Marshals at 856-69","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/16/2026: Anthony Baldosaro · (856) 694-1234 · abaldosaro@franklintownship.com","Township checklist: ABC fire extinguisher no smaller than 2A:10B:C, no more than 10 lbs, mounted in a visible and convenient location","Township checklist: smoke detector on each level, in all bedrooms and outside each sleeping area; battery units allowed","Township checklist: CO detectors in the vicinity of sleeping areas","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/6409/Application-for-Resale-Certificate-or-New-Tenant-Certificate-PDF$t$, $t$https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/151/Fire-Departments$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.franklintownshipnj.org/DocumentCenter/View/6381/Resale-and-New-Tenant-Certificate-Information-and-Checklist-PDF","label":"Official source (franklintownshipnj.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$An ABC fire extinguisher must be no smaller than 2A:10B:C, weigh no more than 10lbs and mounted in a visible and convenient location.$t$, $t$0eef37b7f4a1af24afbf339c1caf12e9516ab758b239407f7a94af869fcc5bd0$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0805.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0805.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0806$t$, $t$Glassboro Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale of Dwelling Certificate (Resale CO); Transfer of Title when violations remain at settlement$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Glassboro Code Enforcement Office (Health & Housing)","Contact: 856-881-9230 ext. 88140 · kharrell@glassboro.org","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Resale of Dwelling Certificate (it includes the Bureau of Fire Prevention smoke/CO/extinguisher application and a rental acknowledgement the buyer must sign even if the home will not be rented) and return it to the Code Enforcement Office, 10 S. Poplar Street, Glassboro, or email Katy Harrell at Kharrell@glassboro.org. Inspections are by appointment only and all paperw","Address numbers at least 4 inches, contrasting, visible from the street","Curb, sidewalk, driveway and apron free of major cracks and tripping hazards","Roof, gutters, siding, masonry, exterior doors, windows and screens in good repair (roof, electrical, HVAC, water heater and plumbing certifications may be required)","Exterior steps, decks, porches, guardrails (36 inch) and graspable handrails in good repair; decks and sheds must have been permitted","Chimney in good repair; certification required if a wood burning appliance is present","Pools permitted, clean, with self-closing gate and 48 inch minimum enclosure","Smoke alarms hardwired or 10 year sealed lithium, working, on every level in a common area","Carbon monoxide alarms on each level in a common area","ABC fire extinguisher, 10 lbs or under, within 10 feet of the kitchen","Stove anti-tip device; bathroom, kitchen and dryer ventilation working","GFI outlets in bathroom, kitchen, laundry and within 6 feet of any water source","No double keyed exterior locks; no keyed locks on interior doors","Walls, ceilings and floors in good repair; exterior grounds clean, no unpermitted fire pits","Also: Buyer rental acknowledgement: The buyer must sign the Acknowledgement for Rental Property and return it with the application, even if the home will not be rented; no Resale Certificate is issued without it.","Also: Open permits and RCA check: The office-use section has 'RCA checked' and 'Permits checked' boxes, so open permits are reviewed before the certificate is issued.","Also: Transfer of Title hold harmless agreement: For settlement before violations are fixed, buyers sign a notarized hold harmless agreement, may not occupy until health and safety violations are corrected, and must correct the listed violations within 90 days.","Also: Sewer or septic disclosure: The application asks whether the home is on public sewer or septic/cesspool."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale of Dwelling Certificate, single unit dwelling (includes one re-inspection)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Second re-inspection (Resale of Dwelling Certificate)","amount":"$35.00"},{"label":"Transfer of Title (settlement before violations are fixed), single unit dwelling, includes one re-inspection","amount":"$125.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.glassboro.org/s/Resale-CO-App-2026-FILLABLE.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.glassboro.org/housing-code$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.glassboro.org/s/Transfer-of-Title-App-2026-FILLABLE.pdf","label":"Official source (glassboro.org)"},{"url":"https://www.glassboro.org/s/Resale-CO-App-2026-FILLABLE.pdf","label":"Official source (glassboro.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Properties are not permitted to go to settlement without proper Resale CO/Transfer of Title.$t$, $t$4ef3ba6891c2faa7e675cbe214751c7df08fc8f5087fd580dba17faeb76b0020$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":7,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0806.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0806.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0806$t$, $t$Glassboro Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Glassboro Bureau of Fire Prevention (Glassboro Fire Department) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-881-9230 ext. 88350 · kdamico@glassboro.org","Apply: Request more than 10 business days before the change of occupant for the lowest fee","How to apply: Complete page 2 of the Borough resale packet, 'Application for Smoke, CO Monitor & Fire Extinguisher Inspection', and submit it with the Resale of Dwelling Certificate application to 10 S. Poplar Street. The smoke, CO and extinguisher inspection is done at the same time as the resale inspection by the same inspector.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 6/16/2026: Steven E Smith Jr · (856) 881-5636 · ssmith@glassboro.org","Smoke alarms must be hardwired or 10 year sealed lithium, on every level of the home in a common area (Borough resale checklist)","Carbon monoxide alarms on each level of the home in a common area (Borough resale checklist)","ABC fire extinguisher, 10 lbs or under, within 10 feet of the kitchen (Borough resale checklist)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request more than 10 business days before change of occupant","amount":"$ 45.00"},{"label":"Request 4 to 10 business days before change of occupant","amount":"$ 90.00"},{"label":"Request fewer than 4 business days before change of occupant","amount":"$ 160.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.glassboro.org/s/Resale-CO-App-2026-FILLABLE.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.glassboro.org/fire-department$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.glassboro.org/s/Resale-CO-App-2026-FILLABLE.pdf","label":"Official source (glassboro.org)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The application fee for a certificate of smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm, and portable fire extinguisher compliance, as required by N.J.AC. 5:70-2.3 shall be based upon the amount of time remaining before the change of occupant is expected, as follows:$t$, $t$3185b9f874346fec551a43b8cb464ccedffd65193c00457364007d7af2a4faad$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":6,"fee_ok":6,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":7,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0806.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0806.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0807$t$, $t$Greenwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (Certificate of Continued Occupancy) inspection$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Inspector / Housing Officer, Greenwich Township Construction Office","Contact: 856-423-9129 ext. 201 or 214 · jgiordano@greenwichtwp.com","How to apply: Fill out the Application for Certificate of Occupancy (mark it Resale and give the settlement date) and submit it to the Construction Office at 420 Washington Street, Gibbstown, with the fee (form lists cash or check). The application is not complete until the owner or realtor calls the office to schedule the inspection: ext. 201 (Kay Hewes) or ext. 214 (inspection officer). Inspections are done T","Yard clean, no trash, debris, junk or junk cars; lawn mowed","Exterior in good repair, no chipped paint or corrosion","House numbers visible from the street (3 or 4 inch depending on setback)","Handrails and guards on all stairways; basement stair openings blocked so no fall-through","Doors and windows in good condition; windows open smoothly, have screens, stay open; no broken glass","Bathrooms have a window or mechanical ventilation","GFI outlets in bathrooms, kitchens and laundry rooms within 6 ft of a water source; at least two outlets per room","Metal dryer vent (no plastic)","Smoke alarm on each floor: 10-year sealed battery unit unless hard-wired with battery backup","Carbon monoxide alarm if heat or hot water is gas or oil fired","Fire extinguisher rated 2-A:10-B:C (ABC)","Water heater in good condition with relief valve discharge pipe ending 6 inches from floor; toilets and plumbing with no leaks; adequate water pressure","Oil-fired heater inspected within last 2 years; wood fireplaces or stoves cleaned and inspected by a licensed chimney sweep","Electric service in good condition, no bare wires or missing box covers; oil tanks not leaking","Sidewalks with no raised sections over 1 inch; sheds, garages and fences in good condition","Also: Open construction permits must be closed: CO checklist: 'CO will not be issued if home has any open construction permits that are pending.'"]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential inspection fee","amount":"$60.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection fee","amount":"$25.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.greenwichtwp.com/DocumentCenter/View/3009/CO-Inspection-Application-rev2025$t$, $t$https://www.greenwichtwp.com/2168/Construction-Code-Office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.greenwichtwp.com/DocumentCenter/View/3009/CO-Inspection-Application-rev2025","label":"Official source (greenwichtwp.com)"},{"url":"https://www.greenwichtwp.com/2168/Construction-Code-Office","label":"Official source (greenwichtwp.com)"},{"url":"https://www.greenwichtwp.com/DocumentCenter/View/933/CO-Inspection-Check-list","label":"Official source (greenwichtwp.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$RESALE: RENTAL: OTHER: SETTLEMENT/OCCUPANCY DATE: ... THIS DWELLING IS NOT TO BE OCCUPIED UNTIL A CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY IS ISSUED BY THE HOUSING INSPECTOR OF GREENWICH TOWNSHIP.$t$, $t$499009723977225a1c9c71b990db2fe3aa01b95307ba6737781a87e43e658aca$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0807.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0807.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0807$t$, $t$Greenwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Greenwich Township Fire Official (municipal local enforcing agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-423-1038 ext. 215","How to apply: Contact the township Fire Official. The Spring 2026 newsletter says fire inspection fees can be paid online through the township payment portal.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 8/13/2026: William C Angelini · (856) 423-1038 · fireofficial@greenwichtwp.com","Township CO checklist (Rev. 6/14/21) asks for a 10-year sealed battery smoke alarm on each floor unless hard-wired with battery backup, and a 2-A:10-B:C extinguisher; these are CO checklist items, not a published fire bureau rule","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.greenwichtwp.com/DocumentCenter/View/3343/Spring-2026-Newsletter$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.greenwichtwp.com/DocumentCenter/View/3343/Spring-2026-Newsletter","label":"Official source (greenwichtwp.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Greenwich Township$t$, $t$ded453d748c61ed99666da72a18c31b6b25391e8dc7a79d6ddeb245955ce2cd6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0807.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0807.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0808$t$, $t$Harrison Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Transfer of Ownership / Occupancy (CTO)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Harrison Township Housing Department (Housing Code Official, Property Maintenance / Code Enforcement)","Contact: 856-478-4111 · property_maintenance@harrisontwp.us","Apply: Apply at least 30 days before settlement. Inspections requested within 10 business days of the application are charged the expedited fee.","How to apply: Fill out the CTO application completely and submit it with the fee (cash or check) to the Housing Code Official's office, 114 Bridgeton Pike, Mullica Hill. Inspectors in the field will not accept applications or fees. After the application is processed, the owner or realtor must call or email the housing office to schedule the inspection. If the buyer is taking responsibility for the certificate, ","Passing inspection under the 2024 International Property Maintenance Code","Smoke detector certification from the fire department (Fire District #1)","Septic certification; if work is needed, written documentation or sealed correction plans, with 60 days to fix under a temporary certificate","Proper permits and inspections for any work done in the home","All utilities on and working at the time of inspection","Certifications may be required for chimneys, roof, electrical, structural and heating","Also: Septic certification: Required for issuance of the CTO; if the septic is not certified and work is needed, submit written documentation or sealed correction plans; 60 days to correct under a Temporary Certificate.","Also: Open permits: Proper permits and inspections are required for any work completed in the home.","Also: Utilities on: All utilities must be on and working at the time of inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Residential initial inspection (covers initial inspection and first re-inspection)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Residential expedited (inspection needed within 10 business days of application)","amount":"$150"},{"label":"Third and each later inspection","amount":"$50.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://harrisontwp.us/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/CTO-applicatiCertification-of-Tranfer-of-OwnershipOccupancy-Application-rev-11242025.pdf$t$, $t$https://harrisontwp.us/department/property-maintenance-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://harrisontwp.us/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/CTO-applicatiCertification-of-Tranfer-of-OwnershipOccupancy-Application-rev-11242025.pdf","label":"Official source (harrisontwp.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$PROPERTY TYPE: ____House Sale / ____ House Rental / ____ Apartment Rental / _____ Commercial ... Please do not schedule a settlement date until the CTO is approved and returned.$t$, $t$9fc92cc44151f63f3a0c96fe49b7b7ab43a6f07aca27d516bde1551d184b4f32$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0808.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0808.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0808$t$, $t$Harrison Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Bureau of Fire Prevention, Harrison Township Fire District #1 (fire district)","Contact: 856-478-0423 · matt@htfd23.com","Apply: Lowest fee applies when the request is received 11 or more days before closing","How to apply: Fill out the Certificate of Smoke Alarm, Carbon Monoxide Alarm and Portable Fire Extinguisher Compliance application (mark Sale, give closing date) and send it with a check payable to 'Bureau of Fire Prevention' to Harrison Township Fire District #1, 312 Ewan Rd, Mullica Hill, NJ 08062, or contact the office by email.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 8/23/2012: Matthew R Cardile · (609) 868-0823 · matt@htfd23.com","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Request received 11 or more days before closing","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Request received 5 to 10 days before closing","amount":"$160.00"},{"label":"Request received 4 days or less before closing","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection for failed inspection","amount":"$65.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://harrisontwp.us/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Fire-inspection-revised-01032024.pdf$t$, $t$https://harrisontwp.us/department/fire-district/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://harrisontwp.us/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Fire-inspection-revised-01032024.pdf","label":"Official source (harrisontwp.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Before any one- and two-family or attached single family structure is sold, leased, or otherwise made subject to a change of occupancy for residential purposes, the owner shall obtain a certificate or smoke alarm, carbon monoxide alarm, and portable fire extinguisher compliance CSACMAPFEC, evidencing compliance with N.J.A.C. 5:70-4.19, from [Bureau of Fire Prevention, Harrison Township Fire District#1].$t$, $t$d438f1c3b1ac64618563bb3165380450bfa183a794c8d0cf032dc3903ea0bfb2$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":7,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0808.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0808.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0809$t$, $t$Logan Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for change of occupancy / change of ownership (Change of Owner/Occupancy Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Construction Official / Municipal Housing Inspector, Construction and Code Enforcement Department","Contact: 856-467-3424 ext. 5","How to apply: Apply to the Construction Official on the township's form. Change of Owner/Occupancy inspections are reported to be held Monday to Thursday, 12:00 pm to 2:00 pm. Call the Construction Department to confirm the current form and fee."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.logan-twp.org/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://ecode360.com/8046096","label":"Official source (ecode360.com)"},{"url":"https://www.logan-twp.org/departments/construction-and-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (logan-twp.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Certificates of occupancy are required for human habitation of all existing dwelling units in the Township of Logan before a change in occupancy of any such unit may be effected.$t$, $t$bdfdde41ad5c4b3c4e388998ba141ef996a2aa8d3343aa4ee6a3f19f3a11511e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":1,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0809.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0809.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0809$t$, $t$Logan Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Logan Township Fire Official (municipal local enforcing agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-467-3424","How to apply: Contact Logan Township municipal offices (125 Main Street, Bridgeport) for the smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate application.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 7/31/2026: Scott D Oatman · (856) 467-3606 · soatman@logan-twp.org","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, null, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Logan Township$t$, $t$6ef498dfab222dce847d4cc1f1e9f53fcc1d7562ac1075ea064fb08846bc7134$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":1,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0809.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0809.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0810$t$, $t$Mantua Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing Certificate (Rental/Resale Housing Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Construction Office (Uniform Construction Code Office), Construction Code Official","Contact: 856-468-9050 · jgallagher@mantuatownship.com","How to apply: Fill out the Rental/Resale Housing Inspection form (mark Resale, give settlement date) and submit it with a check payable to Mantua Township, in person, in the drop box outside the Construction Office, or by mail to 401 Main Street, Mantua, NJ 08051. If mailed, the applicant must call to schedule the inspection. The applicant must also call to schedule any re-inspection.","Meets Township Housing Standards (Ordinance 95 / Chapter 120 property maintenance)","At least one UL-listed 10-year smoke detector on each floor","At least one carbon monoxide detector on each floor, within 10 feet of bedroom doors (depends on the year the house was built)","No open construction permits","Fireplace or wood stove certification and well or septic certification, if the home has them (listed on the form)","Utilities on (asked on the form)","Also: Open permits must be closed: No Housing Certificates will be issued if a property has remaining open permits.","Also: Fireplace / wood stove and well / septic certifications: The inspection form has checkboxes for 'Fireplace/Wood Burning Stove (Cert.)' and 'Well/Septic Tank (Cert.)'."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Housing Certificate inspection (includes one free re-inspection)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Each additional re-inspection","amount":"$30"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://mantuatownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2026-Housing-Information-Form-and-Application.pdf$t$, $t$https://mantuatownship.com/construction-department/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://mantuatownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2026-Housing-Information-Form-and-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (mantuatownship.com)"},{"url":"https://mantuatownship.com/construction-department/","label":"Official source (mantuatownship.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A HOUSING CERTIFICATE is required for any residential sale or change of tenant.$t$, $t$4303cd56dd27c41a7b4d7afc1097e049db9013716973bb6ae9c9122d3390467e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0810.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0810.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0810$t$, $t$Mantua Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Mantua Township Fire District (fire and smoke inspection) (fire district)","How to apply: Contact the Mantua Township Fire District (township website links to mtfd22.com) for the smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 7/1/2026: Daniel R Hauss · (856) 468-7222 · dhauss@mtfd22.com","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$http://mtfd22.com/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://mantuatownship.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/2026-Housing-Information-Form-and-Application.pdf","label":"Official source (mantuatownship.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$(Does not include the fire and smoke inspection they are handled by the fire district at their cost.)$t$, $t$986240c8cf513e43e3c7b5396b73084a18feb075e4887511bdc48c97c4da920e$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":2,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0810.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0810.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0811$t$, $t$Monroe Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Certificate of Occupancy (Resale Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Monroe Township Housing Office (Housing Official Dan Kozak)","Contact: 856-728-9800 ext. 289 or 296 · housing@monroetownshipnj.org","Apply: Submit the application 3 to 4 weeks before settlement. Requests with less than 7 business days cost more.","How to apply: Download the Resale Application Packet, fill out the application, and have the buyer sign the Acknowledgement of Responsibility in front of a notary (the original is required; inspections cannot be scheduled without it). Submit in person or by mail to the Monroe Township Housing Office, 125 Virginia Avenue, Williamstown, NJ 08094, with exact cash, check or money order payable to 'Monroe Township H","Valid for: Inspections are only valid for 60 days","House numbers at least 3 inches on both sides of the mailbox","Smoke alarms on all levels; battery alarms must be 10-year sealed units; hardwired alarms must stay hardwired and be under 10 years old","Carbon monoxide alarms outside sleeping areas (exception for all-electric homes with detached garages)","Fire extinguisher 2A-10B:C, no more than 10 lb, mounted with its bracket within 10 ft of the kitchen in the exit path, top no higher than 5 ft, serviced and tagged within 12 months or new with receipt, manual left for new occupant","Satisfactory lab report including mercury for private wells","Satisfactory septic certification from Gloucester County Dept of Health for private septic","Exterior clean, safe and in satisfactory condition","Pool barriers: 4 ft fence and self-closing, self-latching gate that opens out with release 54 inches from the ground; no stagnant water","Hot tub safety straps in good working order","Abandoned property registration fees and emergency work charges paid","All zoning, construction and Board of Health permits and violations closed and penalties paid","All property maintenance violations satisfied and penalties paid","Buyer's notarized Acknowledgement of Responsibility form submitted with the application","Also: Open permits and violations must be closed: All construction permits and violations must be closed before the CO is issued; all zoning, construction, Board of Health and property maintenance violations satisfied and penalties paid.","Also: Private well test: Satisfactory lab report including mercury for private wells.","Also: Septic certification: Satisfactory septic certification for private septic systems by Gloucester County Dept of Health.","Also: Abandoned property fees and emergency work charges: Must be paid in full before the CO.","Also: Buyer Acknowledgement of Responsibility (notarized): Original notarized form completed by the buyer must be submitted with the application; the CO can be denied without it."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Resale inspection application","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"Request with less than 7 business days","amount":"$300.00"},{"label":"No answer at door for scheduled inspection","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Reinspection","amount":"$25.00"},{"label":"Reinspection with less than 7 business days","amount":"$50.00"},{"label":"Affidavit / temporary certificate of occupancy (buyer takes responsibility for repairs)","amount":"$100.00"},{"label":"Failure to obtain resale certificate of occupancy (penalty)","amount":"$300.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://monroetownshipnj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Resale-App_Cklst_Aff-REVISED-8-3-26-1.pdf$t$, $t$https://monroetownshipnj.org/3-2/department-of-development-housing/housing-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://monroetownshipnj.org/3-2/department-of-development-housing/housing-enforcement/","label":"Official source (monroetownshipnj.org)"},{"url":"https://monroetownshipnj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Resale-App_Cklst_Aff-REVISED-8-3-26-1.pdf","label":"Official source (monroetownshipnj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Resale Inspections take place at the change of each ownership for dwellings in Monroe Township, and the application can be found on the Township website in the forms section. An inspection shall be performed prior to the change of ownership, and a Certificate of Occupancy will be issued following a passing inspection.$t$, $t$c9403e100421b3a5a47c3ed3961d245a0af6b03c2dccc8ddd008c6397eff7cce$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":7,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0811.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0811.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0811$t$, $t$Monroe Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Monroe Township Bureau of Fire Prevention (Department of Public Safety) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-728-9800 ext. 256 · fireprevention@monroetownshipnj.org","How to apply: Contact the Bureau of Fire Prevention. The smoke alarm, CO alarm and extinguisher items are also checked as part of the Housing Office resale CO inspection; the township does not say whether a separate Bureau certificate or fee is needed.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/16/2026: Patrick Mason · (856) 728-9800 · pmason@monroetownshipnj.org","The township resale checklist says all battery smoke alarms must be 10-year sealed units (effective Jan 1, 2019), hardwired alarms must stay hardwired and be under 10 years old, and the extinguisher must be serviced and tagged by a certified contractor within 12 months or be new with a receipt, weig","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://monroetownshipnj.org/3-2/department-of-public-safety/fire-prevention/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://monroetownshipnj.org/3-2/department-of-public-safety/fire-prevention/","label":"Official source (monroetownshipnj.org)"},{"url":"https://monroetownshipnj.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Resale-App_Cklst_Aff-REVISED-8-3-26-1.pdf","label":"Official source (monroetownshipnj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Monroe Township$t$, $t$c0615929b7c47e618abd60afb2726f96f345396ae8ccdea2aea3ccb98042a05f$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":7,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":7,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0811.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0811.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0812$t$, $t$National Park Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy for Change of Occupancy (resale inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Housing Inspector, Property Maintenance and Rental Units Department","Contact: 856-845-3891 · ehagerty@nationalparknj.com","Apply: Apply at least three weeks before occupancy; the borough suggests applying when the house is listed","How to apply: Fill out the Application for a Certificate of Occupancy for Change of Occupancy and submit it with the fee to the Inspection Office at Borough Hall, 7 S. Grove Ave, National Park, NJ 08063. Inspectors in the field do not accept applications or fees. The application is not complete until the owner or agent calls 856-845-3891 to schedule. Inspection appointments are only on Thursdays, 12:00 PM to 1:","Exterior walls sound and weatherproof; house numbers at least 3 inches, readable from the street; yard maintained","Garages, fences, walls, stairs, decks, porches sound; driveways and sidewalks without tripping hazards; no big foundation cracks","Porches or landings 30 inches high need rails with openings no more than 4 inches","Roof and chimney sound (roof or chimney certification may be required); no broken glass","No double-keyed deadbolt on the main door (thumb latch required)","Pool fence with self-closing, self-latching gate that swings out (48 inch minimum, 6 ft for inground); no stagnant water; GFCI for pools","All utilities on at inspection","Smoke detector on each level and outside sleeping areas (battery allowed); CO detector outside sleeping area (battery allowed)","A:B:C fire extinguisher, no larger than 10 lb, mounted within 10 ft of the kitchen","Mechanical equipment working; no excessive peeling paint, loose plaster or decayed wood; no insect infestation","Handrail 30 to 38 inches on stairs of 5 or more steps; every room has an operable window with screen","Electrical free of hazards: no extension-cord wiring, covers on all boxes, at least 2 outlets per room and 1 per bathroom","Plumbing without leaks, toilets flush, tub and shower watertight; heat to all habitable rooms","Water heater and boiler relief valve pipe ending within 6 inches of the floor; flue pipes sealed","Satisfactory drinking water lab report if not on public water","Also: Possible trade certifications: Roofing, chimney, structural, electrical, plumbing or heating certifications may be required by the inspector.","Also: Private water test: A satisfactory lab report is required for drinking water where public water is not supplied."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Inspection fee, per unit","amount":"$ 50.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, per unit (charged for each inspection after the second)","amount":"$35.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.nationalparknj.com/Document%20Center/Departments/Property%20Maintenance/COApplication.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.nationalparknj.com/departments/property_maintenance/certificates_of_occupancy/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.nationalparknj.com/Document%20Center/Departments/Property%20Maintenance/COApplication.pdf","label":"Official source (nationalparknj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.nationalparknj.com/departments/property_maintenance/index.php","label":"Official source (nationalparknj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A Certificate of Occupancy is required in the Borough of National Park every time a residential property changes occupants.$t$, $t$80c0fd25586ac3f2a696a3e2251eae4381b9051ab74545f82c99a44e527afcef$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0812.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0812.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0812$t$, $t$National Park Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Gloucester County Fire Marshal's Office (county local enforcing agency)","Contact: 856-307-7912","How to apply: Contact the Gloucester County Office of the Fire Marshal, 212 County House Road, Clarksboro, NJ 08020. No resale smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate form or fee is posted on the county website.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 11/2/2021: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.gloucestercountynj.gov/1139/County-Fire-Marshall$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.gloucestercountynj.gov/1139/County-Fire-Marshall","label":"Official source (gloucestercountynj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The County Fire Marshal's Office currently is the Local Enforcement Agency (LEA) for the following municipalities: Clayton East Greenwich Elk National Park Newfield Paulsboro South Harrison Wenonah West Deptford Woodbury Woodbury Heights$t$, $t$852a5a15b81c498315d11592d52cc2c0ceae5791a3424d92b67dfe7534a5f6ed$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":2,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":2,"quotes":6,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":3},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0812.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0812.json$t$, true),
