  ($t$0814$t$, $t$Paulsboro Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Gloucester County Fire Marshal's Office (county local enforcing agency for the Uniform Fire Code)","Contact: 856-307-7912 · gcfmo@co.gloucester.nj.us","How to apply: No County smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate form or fee for home sales was found on the County website. Call or email the County Fire Marshal's Office (212 County House Road, Clarksboro) and ask how to request the resale inspection for this town, and whether the town collects the application and fee.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 5/16/2025: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.gloucestercountynj.gov/359/Office-of-the-Fire-Marshal$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.gloucestercountynj.gov/359/Office-of-the-Fire-Marshal","label":"Official source (gloucestercountynj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The County Fire Marshal's Office currently is the Local Enforcement Agency (LEA) for the following municipalities: Clayton East Greenwich Elk National Park Newfield Paulsboro South Harrison Wenonah West Deptford Woodbury Woodbury Heights$t$, $t$4eb2c926b1797556f551d0c4c28cc72cc6c8276e734a0ec5bacdb8f1188a581a$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online","no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":2,"q_ok":2,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0814.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0814.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online; no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0815$t$, $t$Pitman Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Municipal Compliance for Housing and Fire Safety Inspection (sale); certificate issued by the Housing/Fire Safety Office$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Pitman Construction Office (Housing Officer and Fire Safety Official)","Contact: 856-589-2433 · construction@pitman.org","How to apply: Fill out the Municipal Compliance for Housing and Fire Safety Inspection Application, including the Sale section (buyer, sales rep and realty company, settlement date, underground oil tank, open permits), and give a lock box number if there is one. Return it to the Construction Office at Borough Hall, 110 South Broadway, Pitman, with payment by check or cash, or contact construction@pitman.org or ","Smoke detectors present and working","Carbon monoxide detectors present and working","Handrails in place","Water heater relief valve with discharge pipe toward the floor","Appliance and exhaust venting","Emergency exit from a 3rd floor","Receptacles, electrical fixtures, GFI outlets, correct fuse/breaker size, no illegal extension cords","Windows open and lock; screens (April 1 to December 1)","Heating system, water heater and water pressure","Ceilings, walls, floors, interior doors, exterior door and lock","No infestation (mice, rats, roaches, ants); interior clean","Plumbing fixtures, water and drain pipes","Exterior: roof, deck, porch, steps, railings, chimney, fence, gutters/downspouts, siding, trim, paint, masonry, lighting, grounds, trash containers","House number posted","All utilities must be on for the inspection","Also: Open permits: The Sale section of the application asks whether there are open permits and the permit number.","Also: Underground oil tank: The Sale section asks whether there is an underground oil tank and for a DEP number.","Also: Transfer of Title Agreement: If violations are not fixed by settlement, the buyer signs a notarized Transfer of Title Agreement and may not occupy until the certificate is issued."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection, per unit (combined housing and fire safety inspection)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Reinspection","amount":"$45.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.pitman.org/departments/construction___zoning/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (pitman.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pitman.org/Construction/Transfer%20of%20Title%20Agreement.pdf","label":"Official source (pitman.org)"},{"url":"https://www.pitman.org/housing%20inspection%20checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (pitman.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$MUNICIPAL COMPLIANCE FOR HOUSING AND FIRE SAFETY INSPECTION APPLICATION$t$, $t$11ee00f562b9f43e2e3e32841339cf13ed879c2841ee34d5cf9e1b19527aa9e6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0815$t$, $t$Pitman Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Pitman Fire Safety Official (Pitman Fire Department is the municipal local enforcing agency; inspections run through the Construction Office) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-589-2433 · firesafety@pitman.org","How to apply: Use the same Municipal Compliance for Housing and Fire Safety Inspection Application as the resale inspection. No separate smoke/CO certificate form or fee was found on the Borough site. Fire inspections are 'Call for availability' per the Construction page.","Fire official in the NJ state directory, updated 6/16/2026: Ryan Pierson · (856) 589-2433 · rpierson@eveshamfire.org;","Smoke and CO detectors are checked on the combined Housing and Fire Safety inspection (Pitman checklist items 1 and 2)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Combined Housing and Fire Safety Inspection, initial inspection per unit (one application and one payment block cover both)","amount":"$75.00"},{"label":"Combined Housing and Fire Safety Inspection, reinspection","amount":"$45.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.pitman.org/departments/construction___zoning/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.pitman.org/Construction/HOUSING-FIRE%20SAFETY%20INSPECTION%20APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (pitman.org)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$F Pitman Borough$t$, $t$b79e2a104e1777f333f62da0ca4f257ce89cd23196a00fd743844b48c1b2df44$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0815.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0816$t$, $t$South Harrison Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Continued/Change of Occupancy and Certificate of Resale$t$, $j$["Issued by: South Harrison Township Construction / Code Enforcement Office (Construction Official/Housing Official)","Contact: 856-769-3737 ext. 7805 · TACO@southharrison-nj.org","How to apply: Download the 'Certificate of Resale - Change of Occupancy' application from the Construction / Code Enforcement Office page, fill in owner, buyer, agent, appointment contact and settlement date, and submit it with the $100.00 fee to the Construction & Code Enforcement Office, 664 Harrisonville Road, Mullica Hill. Email TACO@southharrison-nj.org to schedule the inspection (inspections Tuesdays and ","Visible 911 house number","Steps, walkways, ramps, guardrails and handrails (outside and inside)","No exterior obstructions or hazards; perimeter grading; gutters, downspouts and splash blocks","Basement or crawl space: foundation openings, secure and weatherproof access, vapor barrier intact","Sump pump electrical connection, backflow and discharge; no mold","No mice or insect infestation","Bathroom venting by fan or window","GFI receptacles in kitchen, bath and garage","Kitchen and bath flooring; switch and receptacle covers; electrical fixtures; panel box and panel covers intact; A/C disconnect","Window glass, working egress windows, window guards","Water heater chimney connection, relief valve and floor discharge","Water pipes, drain pipes, fixtures, toilet mounting, hot and cold water controls","Heating system and chimney connection","Smoke detectors and CO detectors","Fire extinguisher, size 2A-10BC, within 10 feet of the kitchen","Also: Trash and recycling cans: The resale form has check boxes for the number of trash cans and recycle cans."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Application fee (continued/change of occupancy and certificate of resale)","amount":"$100.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://drive.google.com/file/d/16rJRY5Y3-o_2-_YT93zK1770XIzET5V_/view?usp=sharing$t$, $t$https://www.southharrison-nj.org/municipal-departments/construction-code-enforcement-office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16rJRY5Y3-o_2-_YT93zK1770XIzET5V_/view?usp=sharing","label":"Official source (drive.google.com)"},{"url":"https://www.southharrison-nj.org/municipal-departments/construction-code-enforcement-office","label":"Official source (southharrison-nj.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$APPLICATION FOR CONTINUED/CHANGE OF OCCUPANCY & CERTIFICATE OF RESALE AND/OR RENTAL$t$, $t$7319c4b9f48fdb27e5a105c278a5083d329f3bdf9d919f4ad194721efa25bcb3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":7,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0816.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0816.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0816$t$, $t$South Harrison Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire township: issued by South Harrison Township Construction / Code Enforcement Office (smoke, CO and extinguisher checked on the resale inspection) (town fire bureau)","Entire township contact: 856-769-3737 ext. 7805 · TACO@southharrison-nj.org","Entire township, how to apply: No separate smoke/CO certificate form was found on the Township site. The Township resale application lists Smoke Detectors, CO Detectors and Fire Extinguisher (2A-10BC, within 10 feet of kitchen) as inspection items, and its $100.00 fee is listed under resale_co. Under N.J.A.C. 5:70-2.3, where a town has its own resale inspection, a separate certificate is not required but the town may not approv","Entire township: issued by Gloucester County Fire Marshal's Office (county local enforcing agency for the Uniform Fire Code)","Entire township contact: 856-307-7912 · gcfmo@co.gloucester.nj.us","Entire township, how to apply: No County smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate form or fee for home sales was found on the County website. Call or email the County Fire Marshal's Office (212 County House Road, Clarksboro) and ask how to request the resale inspection for this town, and whether the town collects the application and fee.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 4/2/2019: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Township resale form checks for a fire extinguisher, size 2A-10BC, within 10 feet of the kitchen","If smoke detectors are tied into a security system, the alarm company must be notified before testing","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://drive.google.com/file/d/16rJRY5Y3-o_2-_YT93zK1770XIzET5V_/view?usp=sharing$t$, $t$https://www.southharrison-nj.org/municipal-departments/construction-code-enforcement-office$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/16rJRY5Y3-o_2-_YT93zK1770XIzET5V_/view?usp=sharing","label":"Official source (drive.google.com)"},{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/regulations/new-jersey/N-J-A-C-5-70-2-3","label":"Official source (law.cornell.edu)"},{"url":"https://www.gloucestercountynj.gov/359/Office-of-the-Fire-Marshal","label":"Official source (gloucestercountynj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$IF SMOKE DETECTORS ARE TIED INTO A SECURITY SYTEM, THE ALARM COMPANY MUST BE NOTIFIED PRIOR TO TESTING!$t$, $t$99e795e6acef78cf95017193235a3348c1905d2a73e5ddc2593eff915eeca6bd$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":1,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":1,"quotes":7,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0816.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0816.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0817$t$, $t$Swedesboro Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Re-Sale Certificate of Occupancy (C/O)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Swedesboro (Borough office handles re-sale and rental C/O applications and inspections)","Contact: 856-467-0202 ext. 101","How to apply: Pick up a Certificate of Occupancy application at the Swedesboro Municipal Building, 1500 Kings Highway, and drop off the completed application there. Call 856-467-0202 ext. 101 for re-sale C/O applications and inspections. Office hours: Monday 8:00am to 6:30pm, Tuesday to Thursday 8:00am to 4:30pm, Friday 8:00am to noon. No online form was found."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.historicswedesboro.com/construction-co-inspections/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.historicswedesboro.com/construction-co-inspections/","label":"Official source (historicswedesboro.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$1) Borough of Swedesboro handles all Rental C/O and Re-Sale C/O Applications/Inspections 856-467-0202 ext. 101$t$, $t$6d7b44dd214185cf7e0159768a942cbbf8c880045d4b77f065639f9a445a6afa$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0817.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0817.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0817$t$, $t$Swedesboro Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Swedesboro Fire Bureau (Borough fire official, municipal local enforcing agency) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-467-0202 ext. 109 · fm@swedesboro-nj.us","How to apply: No smoke/CO/extinguisher certificate form or fee was found on the Borough site. Contact the Fire Official, or ask the Borough office (ext. 101) whether the smoke/CO check is part of the Re-Sale C/O inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/16/2026: Fred Lock · (856) 467-0202 · FM@swedesboro-nj.us","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.historicswedesboro.com/sweedesboro-fire-bureau/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.historicswedesboro.com/sweedesboro-fire-bureau/","label":"Official source (historicswedesboro.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$M Swedesboro Borough$t$, $t$571403be5b303d8f1eb4afd237c679946158b0b6c04ff31ccd31f1d8f790af35$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["no published fees found"],"verification":{"fees":0,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0817.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0817.json. Red flag: no published fees found$t$, true),
  ($t$0818$t$, $t$Washington Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy - Sale (Certificate of Resale)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Washington Township Housing Office (Division of Community Development, in the Construction Office)","Contact: 856-589-0520 ext. 2231 or 2296 · vorr@twp.washington.nj.us","Apply: Have the inspection done at least 3 weeks before settlement (Housing FAQ). Expedited inspections are available for an added fee.","How to apply: Fill out every field of the Application for Certificate of Occupancy - Sale and submit the original with a wet ink signature (DocuSign is not accepted) plus the fee by check or cash payable to Township of Washington, to the Housing Office, Municipal Building, 523 Egg Harbor Road, Sewell. The office assistant schedules an AM or PM inspection window. The seller's agent may apply. No one needs to be ","House number plainly visible from the street, at least 4 inches high","Sidewalk free of trip hazards","Roof drains, gutters and downspouts in good repair","Windows and doors open easily and stay in place","Stairs, decks, porches and balconies permitted and structurally sound; guards over 30 inches; graspable handrails","Pool fully fenced with self-closing, self-latching gates that open outward","Exit doors open from inside without a key (no double-keyed deadbolts)","No more than 2 persons per bedroom; lofts cannot be bedrooms","Smoke detector on every level; hardwired stays hardwired, otherwise 10-year sealed battery","Carbon monoxide detector near all sleeping rooms","All utilities (electric, water, gas) on for the inspection","Water heater with proper temperature/pressure relief valve and discharge pipe (permit required)","Safe electrical system and covers; no hazards","Dryer exhaust vented outside in non-combustible material; bath fan or window vented outdoors","No plumbing leaks; fire-rated walls and ceilings intact; attic access; all open permits closed","Also: Open permits must be closed: Permits must be completed with the Construction Office in order to pass inspection; unpermitted work must be fixed before the CO is issued.","Also: Temporary Certificate of Occupancy (TCO): If the buyer agrees to take on repairs, a notarized Affidavit for TCO lets settlement go ahead; the fee ordinance lists $125 for a TCO request after the initial inspection.","Also: Well and septic: The sale application asks whether the home has a private well, private septic, Township water or Township sewer; the Housing page links to Gloucester County well and septic records. No sale-time well or septic test requirement was found."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection, sale (includes smoke certification and 1st reinspection)","amount":"$150"},{"label":"Expedited inspection, within 2 days (added fee)","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Expedited inspection, 3-5 days (added fee)","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Fee ordinance: CO inspection portion, first two inspections (plus expedited add-ons)","amount":"$125"},{"label":"Reinspection, each (form: each additional after the included 1st reinspection)","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Temporary certificate of occupancy (TCO) request, after initial inspection","amount":"$125"},{"label":"Penalty for occupying without a certificate of occupancy (listed under Change in occupancy, § 179-73)","amount":"$100"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Application%20Certificate%20of%20Occupancy%20July%202026.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/departments/housing/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/departments/housing/index.php","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/departments/housing/faqs.php","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Application%20Certificate%20of%20Occupancy%20July%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/O017-2026%20Ordinance%20Amending%20Chapter%2080%20Fees.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$179- 68. Certificates of occupancy shall be required for human habitation of all existing dwelling units in the Township of Washington before a change in occupancy or change of owner may be effected.$t$, $t$6da5661d5cf6ab98e78ab5498efab24104f5a7c5366d0e68c0d6ab70933aa905$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":5,"quotes":9,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0818.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0818.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0818$t$, $t$Washington Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Entire township: issued by Washington Township Housing Office (smoke certification included in the Certificate of Occupancy - Sale) (town fire bureau)","Entire township contact: 856-589-0520 ext. 2231 or 2296 · vorr@twp.washington.nj.us","Entire township, apply: At least 3 weeks before settlement (Housing FAQ)","Entire township, how to apply: Apply for the Certificate of Occupancy - Sale with the Housing Office; the $150 initial fee includes the smoke certification. No separate smoke certificate application was found.","Fire District No. 1: issued by Washington Township Fire District No. 1 (Washington Township Fire Department) (fire district). Covers: Entire township (the only fire district in Washington Township)","Fire District No. 1, how to apply: Not found. The district website (wtfd10.com, linked from the Township site as Fire Department) returned a bot-check page and could not be read.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 6/16/2026: Michael Mitten · (856) 863-4000 · mmitten@wtfd10.org","Smoke detector on every level; hardwired alarms must stay hardwired; non-hardwired alarms must be 10-year sealed battery (Township checklist)","Carbon monoxide detector in the vicinity of all sleeping rooms","Homes with a generator, solar panels or battery storage need a 'multiple sources of power' label within 18 inches of the main electrical panel and meter (state law P.L.2025, c.19, posted by the Township, enforced at change of occupancy from 3/10/25)","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Entire township: Smoke Certificate (fee ordinance)","amount":"$25"},{"label":"Entire township: Sale CO initial inspection, which includes smoke certification","amount":"$150"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Application%20Certificate%20of%20Occupancy%20July%202026.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/departments/housing/index.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Application%20Certificate%20of%20Occupancy%20July%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Inspection%20Checklist%20July%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/Housing/Forms%20and%20Resources/Secondary%20Power%20Source%20Identification%20Label%20Memo.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/divisions/dlgs/programs/lpcl_docs/cd_gloucester.docx","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.twp.washington.nj.us/O017-2026%20Ordinance%20Amending%20Chapter%2080%20Fees.pdf","label":"Official source (twp.washington.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$$150 - Initial Inspection Fee (includes smoke certification and 1st Re- Inspection)$t$, $t$12c406aa98e9d79df4a67c72c6cd3dd332be05415ce5c749066b856f0b5eb896$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":9,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":5,"quotes":9,"q_ok":8,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0818.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0818.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0819$t$, $t$Wenonah Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Housing inspection (CO inspection) for home sales$t$, $j$["Issued by: Mantua Township Fire District, under a shared services agreement with the Borough (effective March 1, 2026)","Contact: 856-468-7222 ext. 102","Apply: Apply 10 or more business days before closing for the standard fee. 4 to 9 business days and 3 or fewer business days cost more. Payment in full is required before the inspection is scheduled.","How to apply: Fill out the Borough of Wenonah Fire Safety Application on the Mantua Township Fire District website, pay in full (check, money order, or the district's online payment link at https://www.velocitypayment.com/client/mtfd/index.html), then call the fire district at (856) 468-7222 ext. 102 and ask for Daniel Hauss, Fire Official, to schedule."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Standard, application received 10 or more business days before closing","amount":"$90.00"},{"label":"Expedited, application received 4 to 9 business days before closing","amount":"$140.00"},{"label":"Emergency, application received 3 or fewer business days before closing","amount":"$200.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection, each inspection after the first failed one","amount":"$40.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://mtfd22.com/wenonah-housing-insepctions/$t$, $t$https://boroughofwenonah.com/government/construction-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://boroughofwenonah.com/government/construction-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (boroughofwenonah.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Effective March 1, 2026, Mantua Township Fire District will handle Wenonah’s housing inspections (Co-Inspections) as part of a shared services agreement.$t$, $t$15e1d1313178dea5ceaad0b7f6f96d2ebc490073aac52b03bdbada599a2c6ae6$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0819.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0819.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0819$t$, $t$Wenonah Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Mantua Township Fire District (handles Wenonah housing and fire safety inspections under a shared services agreement) (fire district)","Contact: 856-468-7222 ext. 102","Apply: Same tiers as the housing inspection: 10 or more business days before closing for the standard fee.","How to apply: Same application and scheduling as the housing inspection: the Borough of Wenonah Fire Safety Application on the fire district website, then call (856) 468-7222 ext. 102. No separate smoke certificate fee is published; the Borough lists one fee schedule (see resale_co fees).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 2/4/2025: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://mtfd22.com/wenonah-housing-insepctions/$t$, $t$https://boroughofwenonah.com/government/construction-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://boroughofwenonah.com/government/construction-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (boroughofwenonah.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$You will be required to complete a form that can be found online at Borough of Wenonah Fire Safety Application$t$, $t$47ddc35c7959dc99b93270f2fd1801d72d933b88f9e1015bcbf3363c655e7ca3$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":4,"fee_ok":4,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":4,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0819.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0819.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0820$t$, $t$West Deptford Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Housing Certificate of Occupancy$t$, $j$["Issued by: West Deptford Township Division of Housing (Construction & Inspection)","Contact: 856-845-4004 ext. 123 · avisalli@westdeptford.com","Apply: Not stated. The CO must be obtained before settlement.","How to apply: Fill out the Resale Housing Inspection Application (West Deptford) and send it with payment (checks payable to West Deptford Township) to the Division of Housing, 400 Crown Point Road. The Division then contacts you to schedule. Include the fire inspection form and fee. Questions or scheduling: Alissa Visalli, Housing Inspection Coordinator.","Home must meet township housing rules (Chapters 115, 127 and 178), the NJ State Housing Code and the 2018 International Property Maintenance Code","All utilities on and working at the inspection","All open construction permits closed before the CO is issued","Vacant homes: a lock box is allowed; otherwise the owner or agent must meet the inspector","A separate fire inspection of smoke and CO alarms is required with every resale application (see fire certificate)","Also: Open construction permits: All open construction permits must be closed before the CO is issued.","Also: Utilities: All utilities must be on and working for the inspection.","Also: Settlement-only Housing Certificate: Buyer affidavit (notarized) to finish repairs and permits within 30 days; no occupancy until the final CO."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Housing inspection, initial","amount":"$60.00"},{"label":"Housing re-inspection","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Housing Certificate (for settlement only, with buyer affidavit)","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.westdeptford.com/Construction/Housing/WD%20Resale%20Housing%20Inspection%20Form.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"},{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/Construction/Housing/WD%20Resale%20Housing%20Inspection%20Form.pdf","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$A Resale Housing Certificate of Occupancy inspection is required for all for-sale dwelling units whenever there is a transfer of ownership. A Resale Housing Certificate of Occupancy must be secured by the owner prior to settlement.$t$, $t$2a919d1288ab757eb5d62b201ecee6f3242d3e0364ed30064ad3f726f372a7e8$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0820.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0820.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0820$t$, $t$West Deptford Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: West Deptford Township Bureau of Fire Prevention (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-845-4004","How to apply: Submit the Bureau's Smoke and Carbon Monoxide Detector Certification form (WD Fire Inspection Checklist) together with the resale housing application. Pay cash or check payable to West Deptford Twp. The Division of Housing schedules the inspection.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 6/16/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Ten-year sealed battery smoke alarms (UL 217); hardwired alarms from original construction cannot be replaced with battery alarms","Smoke alarm on every level; basement alarm at the bottom of the stairwell on the ceiling, not between joists","Hallway smoke alarms within 10 feet of all bedroom doors","No smoke alarms in kitchens, bathrooms, near forced air ducts or furnaces, in the dead-air space where ceiling meets wall, near ceiling fans, in crawl spaces or attics","CO alarms in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedroom doors, under 7 years old and working; plug-in, battery or hardwired are fine, but not in switched outlets or outlets at floor molding","House numbers: numerals at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently attached and visible from the street; light post or mailbox numbers not accepted","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate inspection, initial","amount":"$40"},{"label":"Smoke/CO re-inspection","amount":"$20"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.westdeptford.com/WD%20Fire%20Inspection%20Checklist.pdf$t$, $t$https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/WD%20Fire%20Inspection%20Checklist.pdf","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$ALL Rental / Resale Applications will require a Fire Inspection.$t$, $t$58030e9d62a1dd7352c4dca298c6e27679ebb83911c4e2d65a43709483fd139b$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":5,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":0},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0820.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0820.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0821$t$, $t$Westville Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Inspection (Residential)$t$, $j$["Issued by: Borough of Westville Housing & Code Enforcement","Contact: 856-456-0030 option 5","Apply: Schedule as far in advance as possible (the Borough says to allow about one week for scheduling).","How to apply: Fill out the Certificate of Inspection application online (Borough web form) or print the PDF and return it with the $100 fee to Borough of Westville, c/o Residential Application, 165 Broadway, Westville NJ 08093. Checks payable to 'Borough of Westville'. No credit cards in the office; cash must be exact; online payment needs a Customer ID and PIN from the Housing office. Inspections are Tuesdays ","Remove trash and debris inside and outside","Fix tripping hazards on sidewalks, walkways, steps and driveway","Cut high grass and weeds; no standing water","Exterior in good repair: siding, roof, flashing, gutters, foundation; scrape and paint peeling paint","Address numbers visible from the street","Handrail on steps with 3 or more risers; guardrails where the drop is 30 inches or more","Windows open and stay open, with tight screens and no broken glass","Bedrooms need two ways out (a door and a window)","Bathrooms need a window or an exhaust fan vented outside","Plumbing, heating and electrical safe and working; appliances on grounded outlets","Water heater gives at least 120 degree water and has a discharge pipe ending 2 to 6 inches from the floor","GFCI outlets at kitchen sink, utility sinks, bathrooms, sump pumps and outside","Work done without permits must get permits and pass final inspection","Proof of extermination if there are signs of insects or rodents","Smoke alarms, CO alarms and a fire extinguisher (see fire certificate section)","Also: Unpermitted work: Work done without the needed permits must be permitted and pass final inspection."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Certificate of Inspection, per unit","amount":"$100"},{"label":"Re-inspection, 1st","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Re-inspection, 2nd","amount":"$60"},{"label":"Re-inspection, 3rd","amount":"$75"},{"label":"Re-inspection, 4th and later, per unit","amount":"$100"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://westville-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/CERTIFICATE-OF-INSPECTION-RESIDENTIAL-APPLICATION.pdf$t$, $t$https://westville-nj.com/departments/housing-code-enforcement/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://westville-nj.com/departments/housing-code-enforcement/","label":"Official source (westville-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://westville-nj.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/CERTIFICATE-OF-INSPECTION-RESIDENTIAL-APPLICATION.pdf","label":"Official source (westville-nj.com)"},{"url":"https://westville-nj.com/departments/housing-code-enforcement/certificate-of-inspection-application/","label":"Official source (westville-nj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$When a property is sold, rented or a change of tenant occurs, the owner is required to complete a Certificate of Inspection application. Property owners should schedule this inspection as far in advance as possible.$t$, $t$6331a6f4bda212f510d6eb9441f71adca9ed52753b214109b99c4ed21e8b8452$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0821$t$, $t$Westville Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Westville Fire District #1 (Office of the Fire Marshal) (fire district)","Contact: 856-456-9432","How to apply: No smoke certificate form or fee was found online. Call the Westville Fire District office at (856) 456-9432; the district lists a Housing Inspections contact at that number. The Borough's Certificate of Inspection also checks smoke alarms, CO alarms and the extinguisher.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (fire district), updated 9/15/2025: Timothy J. O'Donnell · (856) 456-9432 · Timothy.O’Donnell@salemcountynj.g","Smoke alarms (hardwired or 10-year sealed) must be less than 10 years old; locations that are hardwired must keep hardwired alarms","Smoke alarm on each level including the basement, within 10 feet outside bedrooms, and in every room used for sleeping","CO alarms (hardwired or battery) less than 10 years old, within 10 feet of each room used for sleeping","Fire extinguisher rated 2A:10B:C for residential use, within 10 feet of the kitchen on the way out, mounted no higher than 5 feet with its original hardware, not blocked","Low-voltage (monitored) smoke alarm systems need a letter from the alarm company showing a test in the last 30 days","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://westvillefd.com/fire-district-contacts/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://westvillefd.com/fire-district-contacts/","label":"Official source (westvillefd.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$D Westville Borough$t$, $t$38121af6c5a6f7789282b885dba0ab0861bead6e68a820a014991b9331d066df$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":5,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0821.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0822$t$, $t$Woodbury$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Certificate of Occupancy (housing inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Woodbury Housing Department (Code Enforcement)","Contact: 856-845-1300 ext. 127 · cmiller@woodbury.nj.us","Apply: Allow 10 business days to get the initial inspection appointment and at least 5 business days for a re-inspection. Payment must be received before the inspection is scheduled.","How to apply: Submit the Application for a Certificate of Occupancy Inspection (PDF) with the initial fee to the Housing Department, 33 Delaware Street, Woodbury. Inspections are Monday through Thursday, and payment must be received before an appointment is set. The owner or agent must go with the inspector.","Safe drinking water with adequate flow","Kitchen sink, toilet, bathroom sink, and tub or shower, all working with hot and cold water","Water heater working; hot water at least 120F","Approved garbage containers","Each room has 2 working outlets; no wiring hazards; bathroom light on a wall switch","Bathrooms ventilated (window or fan)","Heat working and able to keep 70F; space heaters vented","Safe, clear exits; basement bedrooms need proper egress","Foundation, roof, walls, windows and doors in good repair, no leaks or chronic dampness","Stairs, porches and balconies safe, with railings","No rodents or insects; window screens from May 1 to October 1","Yard free of trash; lawn, hedges and bushes trimmed; fences in good repair","Interior paint and wall coverings in good condition","Smoke detector on each level and in each bedroom; CO detector within 10 feet of sleeping areas","ABC fire extinguisher (2A:10B:C) mounted in or within 10 feet of the kitchen on the way to an exit","Also: Curbs and sidewalks: For any property sold or transferred, curbs and sidewalks must be installed if missing, or repaired/replaced if the Code Enforcement Official finds they need it, before the CO is issued (City code Sec. 167-20.2).","Also: Water/sewer account: The buyer must notify the City Water/Sewer and Tax Office of the change in ownership right away (City code Sec. 197-33).","Also: Landlord registration (rental units): For rental units, the Landlord Registration Form must be submitted at any change of ownership."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection, per unit","amount":"$125"},{"label":"Re-inspection (follow up), per unit, each","amount":"$50"},{"label":"Transfer of Ownership (option listed on the application form; not explained)","amount":"$50"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://woodbury.nj.us/DocumentCenter/View/2520/Application-for-Certificate-of-Occupancy-PDF$t$, $t$https://woodbury.nj.us/1191/Housing-Inspection-Landlord-Licensing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://woodbury.nj.us/1191/Housing-Inspection-Landlord-Licensing","label":"Official source (woodbury.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://library.municode.com/nj/woodbury/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=PTIIGELE_CH106HOST_ARTIINGE_S106-7INDWUNCEOC","label":"Official source (library.municode.com)"},{"url":"https://woodbury.nj.us/DocumentCenter/View/2520/Application-for-Certificate-of-Occupancy-PDF","label":"Official source (woodbury.nj.us)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$All residential units must be inspected by the Housing Department and a Certificate of Occupancy issued prior to:$t$, $t$399a3481f81a5a0f15b99cfbeafd89138e63b292ec89fcca84973118dd23d1c1$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0822.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0822.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0822$t$, $t$Woodbury$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: City of Woodbury Housing Department (takes the Smoke Detector/Carbon Monoxide Compliance application); Gloucester County Fire Marshal's Office is the registered fire code enforcing agency","Contact: 856-845-1300 ext. 127 · cmiller@woodbury.nj.us","How to apply: The City's housing page says to apply for Smoke Detector/Carbon Monoxide Compliance using the same Application for a Certificate of Occupancy Inspection. No separate smoke certificate fee is published.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 6/25/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Smoke detector on each level and inside each bedroom","CO detector within 10 feet of all sleeping areas","ABC fire extinguisher (2A:10B:C) mounted in the kitchen or within 10 feet of it on the way to an exit","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://woodbury.nj.us/DocumentCenter/View/2520/Application-for-Certificate-of-Occupancy-PDF$t$, $t$https://woodbury.nj.us/1191/Housing-Inspection-Landlord-Licensing$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://woodbury.nj.us/1191/Housing-Inspection-Landlord-Licensing","label":"Official source (woodbury.nj.us)"},{"url":"https://library.municode.com/nj/woodbury/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=PTIIGELE_CH89FIPR_ARTIUNFISAAC_S89-2AGDE","label":"Official source (library.municode.com)"},{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Application for Smoke Detector/Carbon Monoxide Compliance - Download the Application for a Certificate of Occupancy Inspection (PDF).$t$, $t$215c3ec8d0870397c6a836b90bf1e8c70ffaad1b5d167b7ab2e945824854e03c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":3,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":6,"q_ok":4,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0822.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0822.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0823$t$, $t$Woodbury Heights Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Resale Housing Certificate of Occupancy (Resale Housing Inspection)$t$, $j$["Issued by: West Deptford Township Division of Housing, under a shared services agreement with the Borough","Contact: 856-845-4004 ext. 123 · avisalli@westdeptford.com","Apply: Not stated. The CO must be obtained before settlement.","How to apply: Fill out the Woodbury Heights Resale Housing Inspection form (include settlement date, lock box number, buyer and agent details) and send it with a check payable to West Deptford Township to the West Deptford Division of Housing, 400 Crown Point Road, West Deptford. To schedule, contact Alissa Visalli.","Home must meet the housing standards enforced by the West Deptford Division of Housing (NJ State Housing Code and 2018 International Property Maintenance Code)","All utilities on and working at the inspection","All open construction permits closed before the CO is issued","Vacant homes: a lock box is allowed; otherwise the owner or agent must meet the inspector","A fire inspection of smoke and CO alarms is required with every resale application (see fire certificate)","Also: Open construction permits: All open construction permits must be closed before the CO is issued (West Deptford Division of Housing rule)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Initial inspection","amount":"$60.00"},{"label":"Housing Certificate (for settlement only)","amount":"$30.00"},{"label":"Re-inspection","amount":"$30.00"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.bwhnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/2020/WOODBURY-HEIGHTS-RESALE-INSPECTION-FORM$t$, $t$https://www.bwhnj.com/226/Construction-Zoning-Enforcement$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.bwhnj.com/226/Construction-Zoning-Enforcement","label":"Official source (bwhnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"},{"url":"https://www.bwhnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/2020/WOODBURY-HEIGHTS-RESALE-INSPECTION-FORM","label":"Official source (bwhnj.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$The Borough of Woodbury Heights has entered into a Shared Services Agreement with West Deptford Township for Construction and UCC Code Inspection and Enforcement Services and for Zoning Official, Housing and General Code Inspection and Enforcement (Services)$t$, $t$39ffcf3cb74f1020ed59f0644cb1a4c7b8e0246a62ed9a20166089b50776b01c$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0823.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0823.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0823$t$, $t$Woodbury Heights Borough$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: West Deptford Township Bureau of Fire Prevention (serving Woodbury Heights through the West Deptford shared services agreement) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-845-4004","How to apply: Mark the Smoke/Carbon Monoxide Certificate option on the Woodbury Heights resale form (or submit the Bureau's Smoke and Carbon Monoxide Detector Certification form posted on the Borough site) and pay it with the housing fees. Cash or check payable to West Deptford Twp.","Fire official in the NJ state directory (county fire marshal), updated 7/2/2026: Shawn K Layton · (856) 307-7912 · slayton@co.gloucester.nj.us","Smoke alarm on every level, less than 10 years old and working","Basement alarm at the bottom of the stairwell on the ceiling, not between joists","Hallway smoke alarms within 10 feet of all bedroom doors","Hardwired smoke alarms cannot be replaced with battery alarms","CO alarms in the hallway within 10 feet of all bedroom doors, less than 7 years old and working","House numbers at least 4 inches high, contrasting color, permanently attached and visible from the street; light post or mailbox numbers not accepted","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, initial inspection","amount":"$40"},{"label":"Smoke/CO certificate, re-inspection","amount":"$20"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://www.bwhnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/2095/WOODBURY-HEIGHTS-FIRE-APPLICATION-FOR-CERTIFICATE-OF-OCCUPANCY$t$, $t$https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://www.bwhnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/2020/WOODBURY-HEIGHTS-RESALE-INSPECTION-FORM","label":"Official source (bwhnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.bwhnj.com/DocumentCenter/View/2095/WOODBURY-HEIGHTS-FIRE-APPLICATION-FOR-CERTIFICATE-OF-OCCUPANCY","label":"Official source (bwhnj.com)"},{"url":"https://www.westdeptford.com/services/departments/construction___inspection/housing_inspection.php","label":"Official source (westdeptford.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Smoke/Carbon Monoxide Certificate$t$, $t$86fd2fa87c72490dc2b5a5624ba4420d470a976bd17211366b613a7a2151c251$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":false,"flag_reasons":[],"verification":{"fees":5,"fee_ok":5,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":0,"quotes":7,"q_ok":6,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":1},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0823.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0823.json$t$, true),
  ($t$0824$t$, $t$Woolwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$resale_cco$t$, $t$verify$t$, $t$Resale / Continued Certificate of Occupancy (CCO)$t$, $j$["Not confirmed yet: Watchdog could not confirm online whether Woolwich Township requires a resale certificate. Call the office before closing.","Issued by: Woolwich Township Construction Code Office","Contact: 856-467-2666 (Construction Office, menu option 1) · kbarbato@woolwichtwp.org","How to apply: Per the June 2022 form: apply in person or by mail at the Construction Code Office, 120 Village Green Drive, and pay at that time (cash or check payable to 'Township of Woolwich'). Inspections are Monday to Thursday, 11 to 3. Confirm the current form and fee with the office.","All utilities connected and working so appliances and fixtures can be inspected","Homes on well or septic need well and septic approvals from the County Health Department","Also: Well and septic approvals: If the home has a well or septic system, well and septic approvals must be obtained from the County Health Department and submitted to the township (2022 form).","Also: Open permits: The 2022 form has an office field for open permits; unpermitted work on abandoned/foreclosed properties must be permitted and approved (Sec. 143-15).","Also: Township liens (abandoned/vacant/foreclosed properties): A CO is not issued until all costs, assessments and liens owed to the Township are paid (Sec. 143-15)."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[{"label":"Housing inspection, initial (2022 form)","amount":"$45"},{"label":"Re-inspection (2022 form)","amount":"$45"},{"label":"Multi-family, per dwelling unit (2022 form)","amount":"$45"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$https://woolwichtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Housing-Inspection-update-6-2022.pdf$t$, $t$https://woolwichtwp.org/departments/code-enforcement-and-community-development/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://woolwichtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/2020-01.pdf","label":"Official source (woolwichtwp.org)"},{"url":"https://woolwichtwp.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/Housing-Inspection-update-6-2022.pdf","label":"Official source (woolwichtwp.org)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Prior to transferring title to such a property, the Buyer or Seller shall obtain a Housing Code Inspection from the Municipality, and all deficiencies noted in the resulting Inspection Report shall be addressed to the satisfaction of the inspector prior to the issuance of a Certificate of Occupancy.$t$, $t$3825337153dd059f671e0b835b03e39b29d9b117759b1c780d99f8e8f1812184$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":5,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0824.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0824.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true),
  ($t$0824$t$, $t$Woolwich Township$t$, $t$GLOUCESTER$t$, $t$smoke_fire_cert$t$, $t$explicit_required$t$, $t$Smoke / CO alarm certificate$t$, $j$["Issued by: Swedesboro Fire Bureau (Borough of Swedesboro fire official, the fire code enforcing agency for Woolwich) (town fire bureau)","Contact: 856-467-0202 ext. 109 · fm@swedesboro-nj.us","How to apply: No resale smoke certificate form or fee was found online. Contact the Swedesboro Fire Bureau, 1500 Kings Highway, Swedesboro (Fred Lock, Fire Official).","Fire official in the NJ state directory (town), updated 6/16/2026: Fred Lock · (856) 467-0202 · flock@woolwichtwp.org","State rule: a 2025 law (P.L.2025, c.19) dropped the fire extinguisher from the state requirement. Follow the town's current form, which may still list one."]$j$::jsonb, $j$[]$j$::jsonb, null, $t$https://www.historicswedesboro.com/sweedesboro-fire-bureau/$t$, $j$[{"url":"https://nj.gov/dca/dfs/pdf/ANNUAL%20REGISTRY/THIRD%20QUARTER%20LEA%20REGISTRY%202026.pdf","label":"Official source (nj.gov)"},{"url":"https://www.historicswedesboro.com/sweedesboro-fire-bureau/","label":"Official source (historicswedesboro.com)"}]$j$::jsonb, $t$Swedesboro is the LEA for Woolwich$t$, $t$9eaa95822e669bcdeffe2fd49b00ed16df0e35ee2bc32e13c39be7161f7ce207$t$, $t$2026-09-30T12:00:00Z$t$, $j${"checked":{"researched_on":"2026-09-30","approved_on":"2026-09-30","needs_lookup":true,"flag_reasons":["town certificate not confirmed online"],"verification":{"fees":3,"fee_ok":0,"fee_bad":0,"fee_unchecked":3,"quotes":5,"q_ok":3,"q_bad":0,"q_unchecked":2},"source":"property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0824.json"}}$j$::jsonb, $t$Checked from official sources on 2026-09-30 and approved in the NJ Resale Certificate Tracker on 2026-09-30. Source: property/data/municipal-requirements/checked/0824.json. Red flag: town certificate not confirmed online$t$, true)
